{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire","id":917816,"title":"Of Vampirism, Death and Immortality, or do you really want to be a vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-19T23:09:46-07:00","id":917816,"title":"Of Vampirism, Death and Immortality, or do you really want to be a vampire?","content":"I wondered lately why so many people wuldn't mind to become vampires, considering vampiric weaknesses and banes quite a reasonable price compared to eternal life, and was struck by one simple idea. And this idea was so cool and terrible, that I'd like to share it with you, for maybe in your setting you could put it into mouth of some Dragon scientist or Sanctified preacher (well, may be it already was in some manuals, I didn't read them all).<br /> <br /> When you are Embraced, you get immortality, right? Wrong. You just die. Forever. You lie still, cold, and your soul -- if you ever had one -- is forever gone.<br /> <br /> Then your Sire drops some Vitae in your mouth, and this Vitae holds some kind of mystical parasyte, that has no memory, no experience, just self-awareness. And as it fills your body, your brain, it devours your memory, your experience, your personality. It's not that you retain yourself, but get Beast into your soul. No. The Beast steals your body, your memories, your personality. It steals you whole and wears you like a masquerade costume. But as this Vitae-parasyte has no memories and personality of its own, it believes it being you.<br /> <br /> But you personally, you are dead, and gone forever. That's why spreading the Curse is not giving immortality. It is a murder.<br /> <br /> So. Do you still want to be a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-20-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T00:30:34-07:00","id":917850,"title":"","content":"It's always been a horror game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:45:24-07:00","id":918032,"title":"","content":"Ooh I like it. The Man does not struggle against the Beast, the Man is but a figment or a psychological construct of the Beast. A Simulacrum of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:51:18-07:00","id":918035,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the body rejects the Beast unless the Beast creates the Man, in the same way a living body might reject a transplanted limb or organ (there's even rare cases of people becoming convinced that their own foot isn't actually theirs, which can lead them to reject THEIR OWN LIMBS).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:00:38-07:00","id":918040,"title":"","content":"Yepp.<br /> It resembles Strix posession, with the only difference that Strix do retain their own self, and Kindred-true-self dissolves itself into the personality of the posessed body.<br /> And Pijavica birth cycle -- born from blood and flesh, and creates personality of its own -- has a similar ground principle too.<br /> It also pretty good fits into spontaneous Embraces, blood sympathy, etc.<br /> And this theory is very hard -- I'd say even impossible -- to really verify. How can you know if you're you or somebody else with all your memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:12:25-07:00","id":918100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918032#post918032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh I like it. The Man does not struggle against the Beast, the Man is but a figment or a psychological construct of the Beast. A Simulacrum of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If in someone's Chronicle this turned out to be the Truth, the various applications of that knowledge would interesting Scales for the Ordo Dracul. Of course this is essentially the<a href=\"https://www.google.com/webhp?sourceid=chrome-instant&amp;ion=1&amp;espv=2&amp;ie=UTF-8#q=teleporter+dilemma\" target=\"_blank\"> teleporter dilemma</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:21:09-07:00","id":918107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918040#post918040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yepp.<br /> It resembles Strix posession, with the only difference that Strix do retain their own self, and Kindred-true-self dissolves itself into the personality of the posessed body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's why the Strix hate Kindred so much. They're seen as inferior half-beings, kind of the way Ghouls are to Kindred except Ghouls don't think they're the top dogs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918040#post918040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this theory is very hard -- I'd say even impossible -- to really verify. How can you know if you're you or somebody else with all your memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such is the cruelty of the curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:34:06-07:00","id":918115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918040#post918040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yepp.<br /> And this theory is very hard -- I'd say even impossible -- to really verify. How can you know if you're you or somebody else with all your memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, in context of the Chronicles of Darkness where they have supernatural abilities to investigate secrets, unfathomable ancient beings that have the ability to know arcane things with absolute authority, and occult processes that shame the ability of modern science for divining terrible truths.<br /> <br /> How can you know if you're you or somebody else with all your memory?<br /> <br /> You can know based on trusting the testimony of those that have the perceived authority to speak what-is-known-to-be-true, like everything else in life we all take for granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-20-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:37:02-07:00","id":918116,"title":"","content":"As someone who doesn't believe in souls = true identity, I fail to see a downside here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:40:48-07:00","id":918119,"title":"","content":"It's a Thesus Ship Paradox for sure, but you know what this take reminds me of? The Prototype games. Blacklight-Mercer is actually a better man than the human he was made from (until the sequel, anyways). The way he gains power and memories from devouring others makes me think of Diablerie and the Tainted Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:42:07-07:00","id":918122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can know based on trusting the testimony of those that have the perceive authority to speak what is known to be true, like everything else in life we all take for granted. </div> </div> </div>And that's the problem in a World of Darkness overfilled with lies, where every truth is mixed with lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T23:41:48-07:00","id":918466,"title":"","content":"This is pretty much exactly how it works in BuffyTVS. Never was a big fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T01:00:12-07:00","id":918482,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I've read this idea in one of the books. It's very familiar.<br /> <br /> It might help if there's a ghost of the original person. Now, from a metagame perspective, the ghost might have no more valid a claim to the original personality than the vampire, but the characters don't know that. It at least raises the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:22:06-07:00","id":919172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918122#post918122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's the problem in a World of Darkness overfilled with lies, where every truth is mixed with lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hear what you are saying, but it occurs to me our world is filled with less unambiguously True information than Chronicles of Darkness. In our world (by virtue of being subject observers within it) any and everything could plausibly be a lie (or Mage's lingo Lie, or Matrix if you are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wachowskis\" target=\"_blank\">the Wachowskis.</a>) and in Chronicles of Darkness you (as Storyteller) can know absolute Truth.<br /> <br /> The certainty which characters within the realities that make up the Chronicles of Darkness would be able to feel would match our own, if portrayed accurately or with any introspection towards our own condition (or rather the Human Condition).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918116#post918116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn't believe in souls = true identity, I fail to see a downside here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point of the Original Poster is a bit muddled because of terminology so let me paraphrase with different terminology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paraphrase of Original Poster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you are Embraced, you get immortality, right? Wrong. You just die. Forever. You lie still, cold, and your consciousness is forever gone.<br /> <br /> Then your Sire drops some Vitae in your mouth, and this Vitae holds some kind of mystical parasite that has no memory, no experience, just self-awareness. And as it fills your body, your brain, it devours your memory, your experience, your personality. It's not that you retain yourself, but get Beast into your consciousness. No. The Beast grave-robs your body, your memories, your personality. It steals you whole and wears you like a masquerade costume. But as this Vitae-parasite has no memories and personality of its own, it mistakenly believes it is being you.<br /> <br /> But you personally, you are dead, and gone forever. That's why spreading the Curse is not giving immortality. It is a murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought experiment to drive home the point:<br /> <br /> Clone yourself with a perfect copy of your memories, then stare into each other eyes for a moment because you both exist at the same time. Then your clone stabs you through the head because that was your plan before you made the clone to do this experiment with the properties of &quot;the self&quot; because you're a bit of a sociopath (you'd have to be a sociopath to do this experiment in the first place). Are <i>you</i> dead, or is the copy of you actually you?<br /> <br /> The question is not about the emotional state or subjective perception of the copy, but rather what happened to the emergent property of consciousness within the original.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=3546\" target=\"_blank\">Of course this </a><a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=3546\" target=\"_blank\">Lin</a><a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=3546\" target=\"_blank\">k puts this idea into perspective.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-22-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:08:21-07:00","id":919312,"title":"","content":"What practical impacts would this have on the setting if it were true, though? Would that mean every vampire-to-be leaves behind a ghost after the Embrace is done? Would some of the ghosts become Strix out of rage from having their lives stolen, but keep quiet about having been one of the living? Can your ghost-turned-Strix recognize you on sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:06:28-07:00","id":919337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=919312#post919312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What practical impacts would this have on the setting if it were true, though? Would that mean every vampire-to-be leaves behind a ghost after the Embrace is done? Would some of the ghosts become Strix out of rage from having their lives stolen, but keep quiet about having been one of the living? Can your ghost-turned-Strix recognize you on sight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds amazing! It puts the other potential Strix origin stories right on their ear. Like a darkly fracture mirror image of Changeling's relationship with their fetches.<br /> <br /> Also its knowledge to base Scale or Coils on for the Ordo, and shatters the philosophies of the Lance Sanctum as false lies. Would fit well &quot;Scientific Method &gt; Faith&quot; themes, and also supports Transhumanism as a movement as particularly valid since vampires were never truly human to begin with.<br /> <br /> Also bonus: Reason for existential dread for all those that know the truth!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-22-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:28:35-07:00","id":920410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What practical impacts would this have on the setting if it were true, though? </div> </div> </div>First of all, the sense of doubt if you are you. And the reason why being a Vampire is not a blessing. And yes, this strix-idea IS awesomely great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-24-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:39:51-07:00","id":920417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=920410#post920410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, the sense of doubt if you are you. And the reason why being a Vampire is not a blessing. And yes, this strix-idea IS awesomely great!</div> </div> </div> </div>As you described it, though, there's no method to even instill the doubt, and you retain everything you had when you were human, except a soul, which is replaced with what may as well be an exact duplicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:46:25-07:00","id":920422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=920417#post920417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you described it, though, there's no method to even instill the doubt, and you retain everything you had when you were human, except a soul, which is replaced with what may as well be an exact duplicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The process of thinking goes not in the brain of vampire, but in the vitae essence of the parasyte. Your brain is dead and not-functional. Parasyte takes your memories and behaviour from dead and inert neurons, but it doesn't ACTIVATE your brain. It just uses it as a hard disc, not as the processor. The fact it belives being you changes nothing from your point. You just die right before Embrace.<br /> <br /> AND well, the thought itself is quite an easy to be imagined... and resonates well with Lancea Sanctum and Ordo Dracul. The first ones may say your soul is in Hell, and the second ones may say you as-a-vampire have never been the man you imagine yourself. It's enough to put these words in the mouth of one of NPCs, that players are going to listen seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-24-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T01:59:59-07:00","id":920879,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm a simple guy, because I have less of a problem with &quot;the real me is dead&quot; and more &quot;my consciousness has been tied to a primal hungry force that makes angry tazmanian devils look like fluffy lovely domesticated animals and I have to visit that hunger upon those around me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T04:10:54-07:00","id":920907,"title":"","content":"<b>Kirby Jerusalem</b>, cool! For I've been talking to too many people for whom it was a kind of blessing. &gt;_&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T04:51:19-07:00","id":920911,"title":"","content":"I'm with MCN *Shrug*<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, I may as well be a different individual every time I wake up in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:40:36-07:00","id":921063,"title":"","content":"I suppose the real problem is... yeah, this is scary if you know. But how would you ever know this was true? New you believes its you. Old you is dead so can't really know. One case where not knowing isn't scarier than knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T12:49:13-07:00","id":921099,"title":"","content":"The other part is that even if you are not the original you, you are the you that you are now. Why this would matter to the current you is beyond me. I mean it might freak you out for a bit but after a few years, decades or whatever, who cares? You are what you are.<br /> <br /> From another point of view, even if you are the same you as before, you now have the beast clawing at the back of your brain all the time urging you to kill and indulge in its wants and needs. I don't think that qualifies as being the same. I agree strongly with Kirby Jerusalem.<br /> <br /> I think people who don't view the vampiric condition as presented in Requiem as horrible are really downplaying the negatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:06:27-07:00","id":921110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=921099#post921099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other part is that even if you are not the original you, you are the you that you are now. Why this would matter to the current you is beyond me. I mean it might freak you out for a bit but after a few years, decades or whatever, who cares? You are what you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuity, which is why Pale_Crusader brought up the teleporter dilemma. &quot;You are the you that you are now&quot; gets into very short-term Ship of Theseus quandaries if immortal-vampire-you is a corpse inhabited by an inhuman monster that's been tricked into thinking it's you by getting your memories when you died \u2014 it doesn't matter that immortal-vampire-you remembers the same things you did, living-you is still dead and unattached to the web of blood and curses that surrounds and pervades and transforms immortal-vampire-you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T07:02:40-07:00","id":921470,"title":"","content":"Basically you aren't a vampire, you're dead. You don't even know that your body is still running around plaguing the world, you're just dead. You don't know that the vampire thinks it's you because your ass is just dead. You don't become a vampire, you just die and that's the end for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:28:49-07:00","id":921584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=921470#post921470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically you aren't a vampire, you're dead. You don't even know that your body is still running around plaguing the world, you're just dead. You don't know that the vampire thinks it's you because your ass is just dead. You don't become a vampire, you just die and that's the end for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine there would be several redundant ghosts in that scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:35:07-07:00","id":921589,"title":"","content":"I have MS, my short term memory is shot, I have difficult focusing, and need a cane when walking...<br /> <br /> so yes I'd GLADLY take feeding on a diet of blood to be freed of these ailments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T19:21:12-07:00","id":921816,"title":"","content":"What would be interesting is for a sire-to-be setting up an embrace ceremony, with witnesses and attendants. On the big night, the childe-to-be gets cold feet, in front of everybody. Why? Because someone (an enemy of the sire?) told her that she doesn't actually enjoy the benefits of eternity; she dies and her body gets possessed by something that acts like her. Things look less academic on the breathing side of the equation, doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T03:23:46-07:00","id":921924,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of this. An important, perhaps the most important theme in Vampire is coping with your new condition and the moral compromises you have to make in order to survive, which gets significantly weakened in impact if the truth of the setting is that a vampire is objectively not the same person it were in life. Vampirism is horrible enough, and those who don't see it as such are either young, naive and soon to become brutally disillusioned, or on the fast lane to Draugrhood.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Vampire is about the fear of death and what you're willing to do to avoid it - if you're actually dead from the get-go, the exercise loses its purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:56:58-07:00","id":921981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, Vampire is about the fear of death and what you're willing to do to avoid it - if you're actually dead from the get-go, the exercise loses its purpose. </div> </div> </div>Yes. THAT'S why it's all important not to make this statement a solid truth, but a kind of reosanoble doubt. You've agreed to become an immortal, though the fruit proved to be rotten, so you had to somehow manage with it. And suddenly someon tells you: &quot;You've been cheated as all we have been!&quot; and retells you this theory. And you don't know if he is right or mad, and chilly doubt of being not a person you think you are, but just a red-black slime posessing the long dead corpse. Really, even the possibility of it being truth would make me shit bricks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T07:53:46-07:00","id":922005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=921924#post921924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a fan of this. An important, perhaps the most important theme in Vampire is coping with your new condition and the moral compromises you have to make in order to survive, which gets significantly weakened in impact if the truth of the setting is that a vampire is objectively not the same person it were in life. Vampirism is horrible enough, and those who don't see it as such are either young, naive and soon to become brutally disillusioned, or on the fast lane to Draugrhood.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Vampire is about the fear of death and what you're willing to do to avoid it - if you're actually dead from the get-go, the exercise loses its purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily true. The vampire!you still needs to worry about what it will do to &quot;survive&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much like with Promethean. Except you retain the memories/identity of your &quot;donor&quot;. And don't have an out through the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> One metaphysical implication of this over the original surviving is the viability of being separated from the Beast (Golconda?). If &quot;you&quot; are just a person-delusion of the Beast, you can't <i>really</i> just separate yourself from it. Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-27-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T07:57:42-07:00","id":922006,"title":"","content":"Does it truly matter if you're &quot;dead&quot; if your still able to do nearly as much as you could when you were alive... I don't think fear of death comes from &quot;Oh no, my heart isn't beating anymore.&quot; it's &quot;I don't get to do stuff anymore&quot;. For a vampire, the fear of &quot;death&quot; is still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 06-27-2016, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:06:27-07:00","id":922011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=921924#post921924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, Vampire is about the fear of death and what you're willing to do to avoid it - if you're actually dead from the get-go, the exercise loses its purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>With vampire, the fear of death is behind you. Because you've already died.<br /> <br /> From Blood &amp; Smoke, p6. 'Vampire is also about thrilling action and nail-biting paranoia. It's about dying young and being a great-looking corpse. It's about acting out in all of the ways we imagine we would, if only we couldn't see ourselves in the mirror...Vampire is a game about dead people and it should make you feel alive.'<br /> <br /> All those things you hold back doing because you're afraid of the consequences are gone. Something on your permanent record? STDs? Police? Criminals? Breaking your leg trying that 360? You have nothing to fear from those things anymore because you're already dead and those human concerns are beyond you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:06:30-07:00","id":922012,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, as just a theory some vampire(s) in the setting might hold, this is perfectly fine with me, so I think we're in agreement here.<br /> <br /> That said, personally I don't think I'd be able to care much at all about this theory, as it's something I can neither prove nor disprove, and something that doesn't really affect me in the present regardless if true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:14:15-07:00","id":922017,"title":"","content":"Morangias, but would it change your view on the Second Tradition? And the possibility of embracing people to save them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:20:38-07:00","id":922024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=922011#post922011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With vampire, the fear of death is behind you. Because you've already died.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three stages of being dead in Vampire: dead (&quot;normal&quot; functioning vampire), deader (torpor) and absolutely fucking dead (Final Death). You have to work constantly to keep yourself at just &quot;dead&quot;, and the resulting dilemmas make up a large portion of your usual vampire campaign. You're not even close to putting the fear of death behind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:01:46-07:00","id":922038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=922017#post922017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morangias, but would it change your view on the Second Tradition? And the possibility of embracing people to save them?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just a theory? I don't think it would. As a vampire, I can't tell if I'm myself but undead or a magical parasite riding my former self's corpse and acting on my former self's appropriated memories, or if there's really any difference between the two. And if there's no effective difference for me, why would there be a difference for others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:20:08-07:00","id":922108,"title":"","content":"Sounds like something the Strix would spread around. &quot;You're not really human. You never were. Humanity is nothing but shackles wrought from the memories of your body's previous owner. Cast them off and become the monster you were born to be.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:45:23-07:00","id":923992,"title":"","content":"I already dislike being out in the hot sun, I love nighttime, disease and sickness frighten me, I've always wanted to shake off the limitations of my mortal body, growing old and dying is scary. There are reasons why I would consider such a thing.<br /> <br /> Feasting on the blood of the living carries the risk of killing innocent lives, this Beast inside me has its own desires that I may not be able to control, which could harm my loved ones, sunlight is now <i>deadly</i> to me, there are those that might seek my destruction for simply being who I am and, unlike reasons such as sexuality, skin color, or gender, this actually carries a legitimate reason; I'm a walking, talking parasite and potential monster. Lastly, unless I spread the curse to my friends and loved ones, they will all eventually die (unless I ghoul them consistently, but that would be a perversion of our real bonds).<br /> <br /> Fire can kill me in either case, so I won't count it.<br /> <br /> Fact is, the idea is heavily tempting, but my life would change in certain ways that I would probably never be able to change back. Bye-bye family, goodbye old life, assume a new identity, meet these new people (that might have it in for me as I could just be a pawn or something else insane like that). There are many things to consider. Don't let the kiddies that just want the superpowers ruin it for you. If someone told me that I'm not the old me, but a &quot;Thing-copy&quot; of the old me, I'd dismiss it as insanity or shrug and say, &quot;Oh well.&quot; As for if it <b>were</b> the case, then current me that's not a vampire wouldn't give a damn because I just died. Now if ghosts are real, well, I just might become one and want revenge, but that's a slightly different topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:29:46-07:00","id":927081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dreamweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=923992#post923992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already dislike being out in the hot sun, I love nighttime, disease and sickness frighten me, I've always wanted to shake off the limitations of my mortal body, growing old and dying is scary. There are reasons why I would consider such a thing.<br /> <br /> Feasting on the blood of the living carries the risk of killing innocent lives, this Beast inside me has its own desires that I may not be able to control, which could harm my loved ones, sunlight is now <i>deadly</i> to me, there are those that might seek my destruction for simply being who I am and, unlike reasons such as sexuality, skin color, or gender, this actually carries a legitimate reason; I'm a walking, talking parasite and potential monster. Lastly, unless I spread the curse to my friends and loved ones, they will all eventually die (unless I ghoul them consistently, but that would be a perversion of our real bonds).<br /> <br /> Fire can kill me in either case, so I won't count it.<br /> <br /> Fact is, the idea is heavily tempting, but my life would change in certain ways that I would probably never be able to change back. Bye-bye family, goodbye old life, assume a new identity, meet these new people (that might have it in for me as I could just be a pawn or something else insane like that). There are many things to consider. Don't let the kiddies that just want the superpowers ruin it for you. If someone told me that I'm not the old me, but a &quot;Thing-copy&quot; of the old me, I'd dismiss it as insanity or shrug and say, &quot;Oh well.&quot; As for if it <b>were</b> the case, then current me that's not a vampire wouldn't give a damn because I just died. Now if ghosts are real, well, I just might become one and want revenge, but that's a slightly different topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, ghosts aren't the &quot;real&quot; you either.<br /> <br /> Heh. Soul you, Vampire you, and Ghost you walk into a bar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:59:18-07:00","id":927749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=921924#post921924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a fan of this. An important, perhaps the most important theme in Vampire is coping with your new condition and the moral compromises you have to make in order to survive, which gets significantly weakened in impact if the truth of the setting is that a vampire is objectively not the same person it were in life. Vampirism is horrible enough, and those who don't see it as such are either young, naive and soon to become brutally disillusioned, or on the fast lane to Draugrhood.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Vampire is about the fear of death and what you're willing to do to avoid it - if you're actually dead from the get-go, the exercise loses its purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to disagree. While it does modify that theme you mentioned it does not completely undermine it. <br /> In addition, this could be a powerful theme for a chronicle aimed at investigating the concept of identity.<br /> <br /> I also <b>love </b>the idea about the Strix being the original inhabitants of Kindred bodies. The possibilities for a super cool antagonist are endless!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=918466#post918466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much exactly how it works in BuffyTVS. Never was a big fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Aside] Well that is the story that the Watchers and Scoobies believe in. Afaik there is no Word of God stating that this is actually true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:32:38-07:00","id":928471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=927749#post927749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have to disagree. While it does modify that theme you mentioned it does not completely undermine it.<br /> In addition, this could be a powerful theme for a chronicle aimed at investigating the concept of identity.<br /> <br /> I also <b>love </b>the idea about the Strix being the original inhabitants of Kindred bodies. The possibilities for a super cool antagonist are endless!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Aside] Well that is the story that the Watchers and Scoobies believe in. Afaik there is no Word of God stating that this is actually true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't watched the show in ages, but I think that was the big difference between Angel and other vampires - he got his soul back.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I have to admit that the Strix actually being the souls of people who were embraced is awesome. Or perhaps they're fragments of their soul, the fragment that was chipped away to make room for the Beast? Golconda is shedding the beast from your soul, replacing the chipped piece with something else, whether it be reclaiming it from the Strix you gave birth to or replacing the missing piece another way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T17:01:47-07:00","id":933155,"title":"","content":"Vampires can't enjoy the taste of a nice rare steak. Cows aside even bacon is enough of a reason to not be a vampire. i've always been a fat person trapped in a scrawny Asian guys body and can't see the point in immortality if I have to spend Vitae to imitate eating something i can no longer enjoy anyway.<br /> <br /> i'd much rather be a mage anyway, they may not have eternity but they do seem to have much more control over reality. Now if the choice is normal mortal or vampire i think i would still choose to be human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:04:36-07:00","id":934002,"title":"","content":"Isn't the &quot;can't enjoy things&quot; a relic of VtM and no longer applicable? I read it as you can still enjoy food, you just have to spend the vitae and throw it up later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:37:00-07:00","id":934020,"title":"","content":"i am not familiar with any 2e stuff and i could be wrong but i thought in VtR 1e they couldn't taste the food at all, simply imitate eating it to fool others and spend vitae to do so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T05:08:19-07:00","id":934410,"title":"","content":"Under the Solace drug sidebar - &quot;They say the drug makes the dead alive, or close to it, for one night. The body warms. The food has taste, and the wine makes you drunk again. You shed your supernatural powers, and the hunger dies away. For one night.&quot; And under Blush of Life. &quot;Normally, a vampire looks the part of a corpse. He\u2019s pale. He registers no pulse. He exists at slightly below room temperature. Food and drink taste terrible, and immediately cause violent, bloody vomiting. However, with a bit of Vitae, he can fake life temporarily. By spending a point of Vitae, Kindred may invoke the blush of life for a scene.... They can keep food and drink down, ejecting it later in the night.&quot;<br /> <br /> The implication is that, when fully &quot;dead,&quot; food tastes nasty and can't be kept down. When under some mystical effect to act more &quot;alive&quot; you can consume food and drink normally. I think its notable that the Blush of Life section doesn't mention food tasting good, so it could go either way, though &quot;eject&quot; does imply throwing it back up, and the whole &quot;food is unnourishing&quot; theme is rather central to Vampire, so I lean towards it being unappatizing in either case. Its a breaking point for a reason - to highlight that you no longer are sustained by real food, but only blood. So, not only not a Masquerade-ism here, but actually something that's more important to Requiem than Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to spend vitae to throw up the food, or hold it down. You just spend 1 vitae for the Blush and get the effect for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:01:21-07:00","id":996937,"title":"","content":"What is this Prototype crap!<br /> <br /> But to be honest, I rather have that kind of death than something lame and mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T02:16:54-07:00","id":997055,"title":"","content":"A lot of the talk about souls in this thread is kind of confused, given that souls in the CofD are not the seat of the self or consciousness. Beasts have their souls devoured and replaced with a &quot;Horror&quot; and are still the original person. In mage, there are mages who steal souls but leave the person alive. They lose drive, motivation, etc. until/unless their soul is replaced (and isn't necessarily their original soul).<br /> <br /> So if the embrace destroys your soul and replaces it with something else, that doesn't really mean &quot;you died and are gone and something else is driving your body like a car.&quot; It just means you've changed.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't find the question all that interesting as such things tend to suck the drama (and fun) out of Vampire. What's the point of trying to hold onto humanity you never actually really had?<br /> <br /> As a hypothetical discussion amongst kindred, it's fine. As something proposed as the truth of the setting, it's terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:49:51-07:00","id":997168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire#post917816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wondered lately why so many people wuldn't mind to become vampires, considering vampiric weaknesses and banes quite a reasonable price compared to eternal life, and was struck by one simple idea. And this idea was so cool and terrible, that I'd like to share it with you, for maybe in your setting you could put it into mouth of some Dragon scientist or Sanctified preacher (well, may be it already was in some manuals, I didn't read them all).<br /> <br /> When you are Embraced, you get immortality, right? Wrong. You just die. Forever. You lie still, cold, and your soul -- if you ever had one -- is forever gone.<br /> <br /> Then your Sire drops some Vitae in your mouth, and this Vitae holds some kind of mystical parasyte, that has no memory, no experience, just self-awareness. And as it fills your body, your brain, it devours your memory, your experience, your personality. It's not that you retain yourself, but get Beast into your soul. No. The Beast steals your body, your memories, your personality. It steals you whole and wears you like a masquerade costume. But as this Vitae-parasyte has no memories and personality of its own, it believes it being you.<br /> <br /> But you personally, you are dead, and gone forever. That's why spreading the Curse is not giving immortality. It is a murder.<br /> <br /> So. Do you still want to be a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Buffy had a similar concept in that vampires were actually demons possessing human corpses. Most of them didn't have souls, until they used witchcraft to restore Angel's human soul, while still leaving him physically as a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still if you implement this interpretation of vampirism, then it means Belial's Brood is absolutely correct. The vampire is supposed to be the Beast incarnate, they just don't realize it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And also if you use this method, then I'd have to say that no, I wouldn't want to be a vampire. What's the point of becoming a super powered immortal if I don't get to enjoy it? If all I'm doing is handing my body off to <i>something</i> else, then it's not a worthwhile trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:53:07-07:00","id":997171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997168#post997168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If all I'm doing is handing my body off to <i>something</i> else, then it's not a worthwhile trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>This stubbornly continues to not be how souls work in Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:56:03-07:00","id":997174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997171#post997171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stubbornly continues to not be how souls work in Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I admit, I'm not very clear on the subject either. I only focused on the core books, and even then only Werewolf and Vampire. So don't really know how Mages awaken, or the underworld of Geists work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:57:21-07:00","id":997175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997171#post997171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stubbornly continues to not be how souls work in Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. They are Plug'n'Play, and not technically required even at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:11:39-07:00","id":997185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997171#post997171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stubbornly continues to not be how souls work in Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant, since the OP (and the OP is what was being replied to) is explicitly about something else devouring your memories and everything else that makes you you and then setting up shop in your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:16:23-07:00","id":997188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997185#post997185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irrelevant, since the OP (and the OP is what was being replied to) is explicitly about something else devouring your memories and everything else that makes you you and then setting up shop in your body.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, this method is <i>exactly</i> what happens in The Strain.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasytic worms that infect the host and take control of the body, having complete access to all of their previous knowledge. The worms also serve as a neocortex for the thoroughly atrophied brain, literally controlling the body like a puppet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:15:06-07:00","id":997253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire#post917816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wondered lately why so many people wuldn't mind to become vampires, considering vampiric weaknesses and banes quite a reasonable price compared to eternal life, and was struck by one simple idea. And this idea was so cool and terrible, that I'd like to share it with you, for maybe in your setting you could put it into mouth of some Dragon scientist or Sanctified preacher (well, may be it already was in some manuals, I didn't read them all).<br /> <br /> When you are Embraced, you get immortality, right? Wrong. You just die. Forever. You lie still, cold, and your soul -- if you ever had one -- is forever gone.<br /> <br /> Then your Sire drops some Vitae in your mouth, and this Vitae holds some kind of mystical parasyte, that has no memory, no experience, just self-awareness. And as it fills your body, your brain, it devours your memory, your experience, your personality. It's not that you retain yourself, but get Beast into your soul. No. The Beast steals your body, your memories, your personality. It steals you whole and wears you like a masquerade costume. But as this Vitae-parasyte has no memories and personality of its own, it believes it being you.<br /> <br /> But you personally, you are dead, and gone forever. That's why spreading the Curse is not giving immortality. It is a murder.<br /> <br /> So. Do you still want to be a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it turns you into the protagonist from Prototype? That's certainly an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:18:33-07:00","id":997256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997055#post997055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the talk about souls in this thread is kind of confused, given that souls in the CofD are not the seat of the self or consciousness. Beasts have their souls devoured and replaced with a &amp;quot;Horror&amp;quot; and are still the original person. In mage, there are mages who steal souls but leave the person alive. They lose drive, motivation, etc. until/unless their soul is replaced (and isn't necessarily their original soul).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people are larching onto the &quot;replaces your soul&quot; part and ignoring the &quot;you are dead and the thing that animates you is a separate entity that happens to have your memories&quot; part. The latter makes whether or not the soul is the seat of consciousness irrelevant to the discussion. Vampires are, physiologically speaking, dead. The actual seat of consciousness, the brain, no longer functions. If anything, the fact that the soul has nothing to do with consciousness is evidence in support of the theory that the human's consciousness ceases upon embrace and the vampire just doesn't realize it isn't the same person who died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997055#post997055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the embrace destroys your soul and replaces it with something else, that doesn't really mean &amp;quot;you died and are gone and something else is driving your body like a car.&amp;quot; It just means you've changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't, but the fact that all of your biological functions have ceased <i>does</i> mean that you have died. If the soul isn't what keeps &quot;you&quot; anchored to the body, what is? If it's the brain, then you absolutely are gone and something is driving your body like a car. Personally, I'm inclined to suspect the personality must reside elsewhere in CofD, neither in the soul nor the brain. I do have a musing, which I'll spoiler here cause it's kind of a big tangent from the topic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perhaps there is more to the soul than Mages conceive of. Maybe the part that is made up of the five subtle Arcana and causes the Soulless Condition when removed isn't the seat of consciousness, but it's only one part of the &quot;soul.&quot; To the ancient Egyptians, for example, the soul was made up of five parts. The <i>Ib</i> was the seat of thought and emotion, and was contained within a single drop of blood, passed down from the mother, and contained within the organ we call the heart. Sounds a little like Vitae, no? Diablerie does consume the &quot;soul&quot; of the victim, and the Third Tradition does refer to Amaranth as &quot;devouring the heartsood of [another vampire]&quot;. Doing so does cause the Diableriest to hear the intrusive thoughts of the victim. I'd say that's pretty strong evidence that the <i>Ib</i>, one crucial drop of Vitae, could be where a vampire's consciousness resides.<br /> <br /> Another interesting note from the ancient Egyptian concept of the soul is the duality between <i>Ka</i> and <i>Ba</i>. The <i>Ka</i> was thought to be the vital spark, the part of the soul that made the body alive, sustained by food and drink. When the <i>Ka</i> left the body, the person died, and the funeary rites described in The Book of the Dead were performed to allow the <i>Ba</i>, the personality, to leave the body through the mouth and rejoin the <i>Ka</i> in the afterlife, forming an <i>Akh</i>. An <i>Akh</i> could go forth on its own by day, independent of the body, but at night would return to the body, which served as its connection to the underworld. This is why offerings of food and drink had to be placed consistently in the tomb, to sustain the <i>Ka</i> and make sure the <i>Akh</i> didn't die again, permanently this time. We know from the Mekhet Clanbook that vampires, or at least Mekhet, can be created by interrupting a human's funerary rites, causing a separation between the body (which becomes a Hollow, a vampire with no echo, no reflection, and no shadow), and <i>something else</i>, which the Mekhet call a <i>Ka</i>, (though honestly it seems to be more like the <i>Sheut</i> to me, literally the shadow), which resembles the missing shadow and reflection of the Hollow, and feeds on the flesh of the living. It could be that a vampire is a person who's <i>Ba</i> survives within their body despite the lack of <i>Ka</i>, perhaps sustained by the <i>Ib</i> of their sire. In the case of the Hollow, the <i>Sheut</i> for some reason accompanies the <i>Ka</i> instead of the <i>Ba</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps most disturbingly of all, the <i>Ba</i>, the thing that might be the aspect of a soul that makes a vampire &quot;you&quot;, is typically depicted as a bird with a human head...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997055#post997055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I don't find the question all that interesting as such things tend to suck the drama (and fun) out of Vampire. What's the point of trying to hold onto humanity you never actually really had?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is interesting, but in a different way. It's a major thematic shift for Requiem, but examining what really <i>is</i> consciousness can be fascinating. Just because the human who occupied the body you are in died, does that necessarily mean &quot;you&quot; aren't really that person? You have all the same memories, thoughts, emotions, personality. For all intents and purposes, &quot;you&quot; may as well actually be them. Does it really matter that &quot;they&quot; died and were replaced by &quot;you&quot; if &quot;you&quot; are completely indistinguishable from &quot;them&quot;?<br /> <br /> Has anyone here played SOMA? Fantastic game that explores these ideas in really cool ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997055#post997055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a hypothetical discussion amongst kindred, it's fine. As something proposed as the truth of the setting, it's terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I would want to settle on a definitive truth of the setting. I think any theories on the true nature as vampires are best as unprovable hypotheticals for Kindred to discuss. All that said, I think we're largely missing the point of the OP's question by discussing it in these terms. The OP seemed to take as a given that most people would want to become vampires if given the chance, despite the drawbacks, and was proposing this as &quot;would you <i>still</i> want to become a vampire if there was a chance it worked this way?&quot; To that, I say no, but I wouldn't want to become a vampire anyway. When I was in high school I would have jumped on the chance, but nobody said teenagers have good judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:43:32-07:00","id":997278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997256#post997256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of people are larching onto the &quot;replaces your soul&quot; part and ignoring the &quot;you are dead and the thing that animates you is a separate entity that happens to have your memories&quot; part. The latter makes whether or not the soul is the seat of consciousness irrelevant to the discussion. Vampires are, physiologically speaking, dead. The actual seat of consciousness, the brain, no longer functions. If anything, the fact that the soul has nothing to do with consciousness is evidence in support of the theory that the human's consciousness ceases upon embrace and the vampire just doesn't realize it isn't the same person who died.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what I was getting at, re: people latching on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997256#post997256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it doesn't, but the fact that all of your biological functions have ceased <i>does</i> mean that you have died. If the soul isn't what keeps &quot;you&quot; anchored to the body, what is? If it's the brain, then you absolutely are gone and something is driving your body like a car. Personally, I'm inclined to suspect the personality must reside elsewhere in CofD, neither in the soul nor the brain. I do have a musing, which I'll spoiler here cause it's kind of a big tangent from the topic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perhaps there is more to the soul than Mages conceive of. Maybe the part that is made up of the five subtle Arcana and causes the Soulless Condition when removed isn't the seat of consciousness, but it's only one part of the &quot;soul.&quot; To the ancient Egyptians, for example, the soul was made up of five parts. The <i>Ib</i> was the seat of thought and emotion, and was contained within a single drop of blood, passed down from the mother, and contained within the organ we call the heart. Sounds a little like Vitae, no? Diablerie does consume the &quot;soul&quot; of the victim, and the Third Tradition does refer to Amaranth as &quot;devouring the heartsood of [another vampire]&quot;. Doing so does cause the Diableriest to hear the intrusive thoughts of the victim. I'd say that's pretty strong evidence that the <i>Ib</i>, one crucial drop of Vitae, could be where a vampire's consciousness resides.<br /> <br /> Another interesting note from the ancient Egyptian concept of the soul is the duality between <i>Ka</i> and <i>Ba</i>. The <i>Ka</i> was thought to be the vital spark, the part of the soul that made the body alive, sustained by food and drink. When the <i>Ka</i> left the body, the person died, and the funeary rites described in The Book of the Dead were performed to allow the <i>Ba</i>, the personality, to leave the body through the mouth and rejoin the <i>Ka</i> in the afterlife, forming an <i>Akh</i>. An <i>Akh</i> could go forth on its own by day, independent of the body, but at night would return to the body, which served as its connection to the underworld. This is why offerings of food and drink had to be placed consistently in the tomb, to sustain the <i>Ka</i> and make sure the <i>Akh</i> didn't die again, permanently this time. We know from the Mekhet Clanbook that vampires, or at least Mekhet, can be created by interrupting a human's funerary rites, causing a separation between the body (which becomes a Hollow, a vampire with no echo, no reflection, and no shadow), and <i>something else</i>, which the Mekhet call a <i>Ka</i>, (though honestly it seems to be more like the <i>Sheut</i> to me, literally the shadow), which resembles the missing shadow and reflection of the Hollow, and feeds on the flesh of the living. It could be that a vampire is a person who's <i>Ba</i> survives within their body despite the lack of <i>Ka</i>, perhaps sustained by the <i>Ib</i> of their sire. In the case of the Hollow, the <i>Sheut</i> for some reason accompanies the <i>Ka</i> instead of the <i>Ba</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps most disturbingly of all, the <i>Ba</i>, the thing that might be the aspect of a soul that makes a vampire &quot;you&quot;, is typically depicted as a bird with a human head...</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it follows that if the brain is the seat of consciousness then you have absolutely died and something is driving your body like a car. People have been clinically dead for longer periods of time than the embrace <i>typically</i> requires (setting aside vampires who rise from their graves and revenants for the moment) and they're not driven around by something else. I don't think there's any reason to assume that brain death - as brief as it generally is - would do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997256#post997256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is interesting, but in a different way. It's a major thematic shift for Requiem, but examining what really <i>is</i> consciousness can be fascinating. Just because the human who occupied the body you are in died, does that necessarily mean &quot;you&quot; aren't really that person? You have all the same memories, thoughts, emotions, personality. For all intents and purposes, &quot;you&quot; may as well actually be them. Does it really matter that &quot;they&quot; died and were replaced by &quot;you&quot; if &quot;you&quot; are completely indistinguishable from &quot;them&quot;?<br /> <br /> Has anyone here played SOMA? Fantastic game that explores these ideas in really cool ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played but haven't yet finished SOMA.<br /> <br /> I don't think the question is really interesting, simply because Vampire loses a lot of the drama and meaning if vampires are simply parasites assuming the people's identities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997256#post997256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I would want to settle on a definitive truth of the setting. I think any theories on the true nature as vampires are best as unprovable hypotheticals for Kindred to discuss. All that said, I think we're largely missing the point of the OP's question by discussing it in these terms. The OP seemed to take as a given that most people would want to become vampires if given the chance, despite the drawbacks, and was proposing this as &quot;would you <i>still</i> want to become a vampire if there was a chance it worked this way?&quot; To that, I say no, but I wouldn't want to become a vampire anyway. When I was in high school I would have jumped on the chance, but nobody said teenagers have good judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I wouldn't want to play or run Vampire if there's a chance that it works that way. Which is why I'm glad Requiem doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> As a philosophical question for vampires to ponder it's one thing, but to propose &quot;This is how it works&quot; is a waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:57:12-07:00","id":997319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997278#post997278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's what I was getting at, re: people latching on.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997278#post997278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it follows that if the brain is the seat of consciousness then you have absolutely died and something is driving your body like a car. People have been clinically dead for longer periods of time than the embrace <i>typically</i> requires (setting aside vampires who rise from their graves and revenants for the moment) and they're not driven around by something else. I don't think there's any reason to assume that brain death - as brief as it generally is - would do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brain death during the Embrace may be fairly brief, but brain death during being a vampire is rather longer. Indefinite, in fact. When not under the effects of the Blush of Life, a vampire's organs, including their brain, don't function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997278#post997278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played but haven't yet finished SOMA.<br /> <br /> I don't think the question is really interesting, simply because Vampire loses a lot of the drama and meaning if vampires are simply parasites assuming the people's identities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just don't see anything simple about parasites assuming the humans identities when the parasites themselves believe they are the same person. But, if it doesn't interest you, that's cool. That's why I agree that it should be something characters might muse over, rather than something that is definitively true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997278#post997278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I wouldn't want to play or run Vampire if there's a chance that it works that way. Which is why I'm glad Requiem doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't really see any proof in Requiem one way or the other. It doesn't have to work that way, but there's also nothing preventing it from working that way if that's how you want it to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997278#post997278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a philosophical question for vampires to ponder it's one thing, but to propose &amp;quot;This is how it works&amp;quot; is a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, I don't think that's what the OP was doing. I think they were asking &quot;would you want to become a vampire if there was a chance it might work this way?&quot; and proposing that using it as an in-character hypothesis held by some extremist character (whether or not it's true) might be a source of horror for those to whom the answer is no. YMMV on if that would actually be horrifying, or even interesting. But I didn't get the impression of &quot;what if it works this way?&quot; from the OP, so much as a weird &quot;take that, people who think it would be cool to be a vampire!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:15:43-07:00","id":997336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997256#post997256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was in high school I would have jumped on the chance, but nobody said teenagers have good judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a fair amount of Manga and cartoons may disagree with you, there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T13:39:41-07:00","id":997346,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the real horror of Vampire comes less from the metaphysical condition being soulless and more of the fact that you're an undead monster that well likely spend his nights physical assaulting, mentally manipulating, and outright killing your former fellow man.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, if a doctor (or a priest, I guess) told me that my mother had lost her soul, but would otherwise act and behave in the exact same way that she has beforehand I'm pretty sure I'd get over her being soulless really quick. The fact that souls exist in the first might throw me for a loop though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:32:12-07:00","id":997406,"title":"","content":"Read a nice story that dealt, briefly, with some of it called the <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Night-Cyclist-Tor-com-Original-ebook/dp/B01L7B9VE6/\" target=\"_blank\">Night Cyclist</a>. But really it's something most books about vampires get into. I don't believe you lose your soul in in-game terms, and in real life that's not a problem, but you are for sure losing some of your Humanity, and you're going to spend most of your time around other beings that are somewhere between Humanity and Beast and never really at either extreme.<br /> <br /> They're all going to be dealing with it differently, and people have a hard time with being around people who are different, especially if it flies in the face of your own beliefs. It's hard, doing that social stuff with other vampires, but it's all you really have.<br /> <br /> And of course the blood. I imagine you get over that quick, but that only serves to make clear the difference and distance between you and humans. They're food, now.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i2.wp.com/www.tor.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/nightcyclist_full.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-02-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:02:46-07:00","id":997471,"title":"","content":"Whenever I see this thread I always think back to this comic: <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=3546\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=3546</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:15:52-07:00","id":997479,"title":"","content":"I think it would be an interesting viewpoint, rather than a scary one.<br /> <br /> I don't suppose we have any antinatalists here, who could share their views on undeath and vampiric immortality? While life cannot be undone, the vampire condition does seem to alleviate a lot of their concerns, even if it shares some roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:17:48-07:00","id":997502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997346#post997346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI mean, if a doctor (or a priest, I guess) told me that my mother had lost her soul, but would otherwise act and behave in the exact same way that she has beforehand I'm pretty sure I'd get over her being soulless really quick. The fact that souls exist in the first might throw me for a loop though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the soul part isn't really the issue so much as the dead part. If a doctor told you that you had a month to live, but that they could program an AI with all of your memories and personality and hook it up to your body in such a way that it could control all of your motor functions and prevent decomposition, how quickly would you get over the fact that you're going to die in a month or less?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-02-2016, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:30:52-07:00","id":997529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997502#post997502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how quickly would you get over the fact that you're going to die in a month or less?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably rather fast, faster if the AI was turned on before I died. I mean, parts of people are dying over and over and over and being replaced over and over. So what if flesh me is dead, flesh me has already effectively died many times already. Though I've got a rather odd perspective when it comes to philosophy according to most people I've talked to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:44:23-07:00","id":997536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997529#post997529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably rather fast, faster if the AI was turned on before I died. I mean, parts of people are dying over and over and over and being replaced over and over. So what if flesh me is dead, flesh me has already effectively died many times already. Though I've got a rather odd perspective when it comes to philosophy according to most people I've talked to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair answer. Like I said, YMMV on if it's horrifying or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:30:04-07:00","id":997629,"title":"","content":"A note - Brookshaw has just established that (non-mage) supernaturals don't get Onerios. So, given that Onerios = inside of souls, we could say that vampires don't have souls!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:38:22-07:00","id":997630,"title":"","content":"Not the same souls as mages and humans (and Beasts?) at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:22:40-07:00","id":997639,"title":"","content":"On top of Dave Brookshaw's posts, any effects that explicitly affects the soul can only affect the souls of humans and mages (when described in books handling other supernaturals). Whatever vampires and other supernatural creatures have instead of a soul (and they should have something since they don't suffer from being soulless) is probably so different from actual souls that I think new terminology is required. I see the confusion arise in every single thread that discusses souls and their equivalences.<br /> I really hope the crossover book will deal with this subject. At least explicitly mention that souls are unique to humans and mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T05:36:26-07:00","id":997642,"title":"","content":"The longest period of time most people can be clinically dead without suffering long term brain damage is 10 minutes.<br /> <br /> The embrace, as I understand it, can be used on anybody who has died within the last 24 hours. Which is a significant time gap between ordinary resuscitation.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't matter, because the vampire doesn't need their bodily organs to be in working condition. They're animated through some sort of mystical power (vitae). Or in this case, whatever parasite happens to be infecting them at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, besides, how does somebody really define humanity, anyways?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o8C9jJNif0A\" data-code=\"o8C9jJNif0A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/o8C9jJNif0A/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-03-2016, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:32:16-07:00","id":997660,"title":"","content":"Vampires explicitly have souls, it's what gets eaten during Diablerie. They just don't have <i>human</i> souls. Something about the Embrace alters the soul enough that it no longer has an Oneiros. This is part of why I favor the ancient Egyptian fivefold soul interpretation. Vampires probably don't have Ka, which is probably the part of the soul that contains the Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T06:47:54-07:00","id":997666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997660#post997660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires explicitly have souls, it's what gets eaten during Diablerie. They just don't have <i>human</i> souls. Something about the Embrace alters the soul enough that it no longer has an Oneiros. This is part of why I favor the ancient Egyptian fivefold soul interpretation. Vampires probably don't have Ka, which is probably the part of the soul that contains the Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they have <i>something</i> that gets eaten during Diablerie - whether or not it could be called a soul is academic (literally - it is probably the subject of in universe academic papers). Perhaps it is merely the Strix-like Curse that animates them? Strix don't have souls, but do eat each other like with Diablerie too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:28:14-07:00","id":997717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997666#post997666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they have <i>something</i> that gets eaten during Diablerie - whether or not it could be called a soul is academic (literally - it is probably the subject of in universe academic papers). Perhaps it is merely the Strix-like Curse that animates them? Strix don't have souls, but do eat each other like with Diablerie too...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's *called* a soul in the text. Again, it's probably not the same thing as Mages mean by &quot;soul&quot;. But it's what vampires call a soul. Cue comparisons to how many different things are called demons in-universe and how many mechanical meanings the word reach has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:48:03-07:00","id":997729,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of interpretation I think, although yes, it says &quot;soul&quot; in the text. My interpretation is that it is the vampiric essence, the curse that animates the body, that is eaten. I guess you could call it a soul.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic, I am not a fan of the embraced human being killed in the process. It takes away from the horror of being a vampire because you are not here to see yourself anymore. However, I like the idea of the human consciousness being slowly eaten, or decaying as Humanity erodes. So you don't &quot;die&quot; after the Embrace, but you die as your Requiem progresses and as your Humanity declines, leaving only the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:57:04-07:00","id":997750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997717#post997717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's *called* a soul in the text. Again, it's probably not the same thing as Mages mean by &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot;. But it's what vampires call a soul. Cue comparisons to how many different things are called demons in-universe and how many mechanical meanings the word reach has.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'd prefer a change in terminology or explicit confirmation that they are not the same thing. All the different kinds of demons are pretty well defined so there's no confusion for the players while there's little to no explanation of souls in the books so we have to go on mechanical differences and the words of the developers on the subject. One kind of demon was actually renamed (goetic demon into Goetia) just to avoid confusion despite how well defined they were. The fact that souls lack this kind of expmicit distinction makes it more important to introduce an alternative terminology for discussions relating to multiple game lines (or even just vampires and humans/ghouls).<br /> <br /> While the soul equivalent of a vampire might be a maimed version of a human's soul, I believe it's more than just maimed; mechanically it's almost identical to Strix except it can't manifest without a body the way Strix can.<br /> My personal theory at the moment (this will most likely change as I think more about it) is that the Embrace maims and reshapes the original human soul (which helps explain why other supernaturals can't be embraced, and why it's such a toll on a vampire's Humanity compared to other atrocious acts that are only Breaking Points instead of automatic Humanity loss) to become something similar to what the Strix are. This process is incomplete as the vampire experiences a duality between their Humanity and the Beast. Should they manage to somehow &quot;purify&quot; their soul equivalent from the remains of their human origin (beyond the point of just becoming Draugr; they need to find a way to continue existing without the support of their previously human shell) they themselves can become Strix.<br /> Worded differently: The Strix are the real vampires. Vampires are human/vampire hybrids trying to balance what they used to be (their Humanity) with the incomplete process of what they almost became (their Beast).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:19:44-07:00","id":997817,"title":"","content":"I rather think Strix are <i>incomplete</i> vampires, lacking the human elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:21:31-07:00","id":997854,"title":"","content":"Strix are incomplete vampires, but they're complete Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:26:40-07:00","id":997857,"title":"","content":"No argument there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:12:55-07:00","id":997881,"title":"","content":"I'm personally not a fan of the idea that all vampires' souls/beasts/etc. are Strix. It's fine for the Strix to claim so. It's even fine if it's sometimes the case. But for them all to be seems decidedly un-CofD to me. Too easy of an answer, nothing in CofD is that tidy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:57:13-07:00","id":997897,"title":"","content":"My theory isn't that the Beast is a Strix. It's that the Beast is the humans soul twisted into something that could've become a Strix if the Embrace wasn't an incomplete process for it. (A Strix can create another Strix, but a vampire can only create other vampires.) The Beast is all the instincts and drives of predators, while the Strix are consciousnesses. A continuation of my theory is that the Beast is created from Humanity's knowledge of predatory behaviour (in both predators and humans) which keeps it from becoming a Strix because it's marked by Humanity even if the vampire becomes a Draugr.<br /> I don't know how to best explain my idea (an I'm honestly not as stoked about it anymore), but I do know it sounds like an awesome in-character theory for a Dragon developing a highly heretical Coil based on &quot;refining&quot; themselves further in order to become a Strix.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry if it sounds like rambling, but I'm posting on my phone and it's hard to see if I'm writing coherently when only a single line is visible at a time while the keyboard is up. I'll try to keep myself to my computer when posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-03-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:35:47-07:00","id":997976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=997630#post997630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the same souls as mages and humans (and Beasts?) at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. The book repeatedly mentions vampire souls. 'Suffering unnatural lust towards a Serpent? Just look into her soul. Clears that right up.' 'They devoured the writhing god that lived there, tasting the immaculate slime. Divinity changed their souls and bodies.' 'You are an avatar of disgust. Dread and discomfort oozes from you, scabbing everything over in the putrid film of your rotting soul's exhaust.' 'The Blood is mutable and takes on many shapes, filling the hollows that humanity carves into its soul.' 'Through the incestuous cycle of Embrace and Amaranth, each survivor was a walking mass grave, teeming with the forfeit souls of the devoured.' About a possibility rumor about the VII, 'Joining brings with it terrible consequences, perhaps even the bartering of its members' souls.' 'He who devours a vampire's heartsblood also devours the soul.' 'diablerie; draining another vampire of not only his blood but his soul.' 'Once the sun rises, the vampire's soul drags her toward slumber.' On diablerie, 'Once the victim's Health boxes are full of aggravated damage, the victim's very soul struggles against his assailant as he reaches Final Death.' 'Most Kindred will kill a human at some point during her Requiem, but Amaranth is far more than extinguishing a life: It's the willful destruction of a soul. While modern, secular minds often eschew the existence of a soul, a diablerist will never deny its existence.'<br /> <br /> It goes on like this. It's not just 'fluff,' it goes into it in the mechanical sections as well. The one mention of a vampire being soulless is in the character concepts section of the Invictus, where it suggests a 'soulless bureaucrat,' and it's safe to say that this is just being flowery with words. Not only is the existence of the vampire's soul very clear, doubt about it is never even brought up.<br /> <br /> The idea of a vampire not having a soul exists in media, but not in this media. If you want to play that in your games, great, but in the setting of Vampire the Requiem it is very clear that they do. It's not the same as the soul of an ordinary, living person, but it is a soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-03-2016, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:40:18-07:00","id":998113,"title":"","content":"Notably, the core blue book describes Integrity as measuring the health of a soul. It's possible that templates with Integrity replacements measure the health of a soul that has somehow been changed. Humanity measures the health of a soul that is &quot;rotting&quot;, as Nofather's quote puts it. Harmony measures the health of a soul that is half spirit. Wisdom measures the health of a soul that has touched the Supernal. Pilgrimage measures the health of a soul in the making. Clarity measures the health of a soul that has been reshaped first by the gentry and then by its owner, and further maimed by the brambles of the Hedge. Cover measures the health of a soul that has been re-purposed for use as a disgise for a fallen Angel. Satiety measures the health of a soul that has been consumed by a Horror? I don't know Beast very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:12:14-07:00","id":998122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998113#post998113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity measures the health of a soul that has been reshaped first by the gentry and then by its owner, and further maimed by the brambles of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that changelings had their souls ripped out by huntsmen as part of making their fetch?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satiety measures the health of a soul that has been consumed by a Horror? I don't know Beast very well. </div> </div> </div>As the horror is the beasts soul, satiety does describe the status of the beast's soul. Though describe it's hunger rather than it's health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-04-2016, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T05:52:01-07:00","id":998194,"title":"","content":"As has been mentioned multiple times, how bad this is really depends on what you consider the self. If Mage is to be believed, Mind is its own thing, separate from the physical brain and whatever it is that a soul is. Generally, the thing we (or at least I) consider the self seems to be the Mind, which for all intents and purposes remains intact even after death in the case of vampirism. I mean what is it about death that's scary? Imo, it's that we stop and never start again regardless of whether we want to or not. The self vanishes, or at the very least loses its ability to act upon the world. If all death was was a stopping of our hearts and bodily functions and what not, while retaining the ability to move around, interact, and maintain the part of you that makes you you (personality, manner of thinking/acting/ etc.) we probably wouldn't be nearly as afraid of death as we are, it would just be another stage of life honestly. So you could say that the Beast eats your memories or whatever and just thinks it's you, but regardless, your Mind essentially remains the same. What makes you you remains the same. There are a few changes, but people already change when certain stimuli is introduced into their existence, and this isn't really that much different.<br /> <br /> So you can say that you died, but really, how did you die? Your physical body stopped working the way it used to, but who cares? The scary part of death has been taken away. The body (or soul, or whatever) housing your consciousness has changed, but the consciousness still remains. That consciousness might now be housed by a vampiric Beast now rather than an natural human soul (whatever the hell that even is), but it remains the same, with maybe an acceptable level of change that is honestly expected as we grow and experience certain things. <br /> <br /> That said, if your definition of self includes that substance? object? existence? of the thing known as a human soul then of course things might be a bit more disconcerting for you. But then again, all the supernaturals have to deal with that. Even mages, the most human like of the splats has an inhuman soul. I guess you could also argue that they're close enough to have oneroi but it isn't like most people actively realize that's a thing, so the loss of it is pretty negligible as far as normal life/existence is concerned. <br /> <br /> And I just woke up enough to realize I'm rambling, time to go get some coffee or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:37:41-07:00","id":998220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998113#post998113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, the core blue book describes Integrity as measuring the health of a soul. It's possible that templates with Integrity replacements measure the health of a soul that has somehow been changed. Humanity measures the health of a soul that is &quot;rotting&quot;, as Nofather's quote puts it. Harmony measures the health of a soul that is half spirit. Wisdom measures the health of a soul that has touched the Supernal. Pilgrimage measures the health of a soul in the making. Clarity measures the health of a soul that has been reshaped first by the gentry and then by its owner, and further maimed by the brambles of the Hedge. Cover measures the health of a soul that has been re-purposed for use as a disgise for a fallen Angel. Satiety measures the health of a soul that has been consumed by a Horror? I don't know Beast very well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humanity measures how much empathy and perspective you have towards humans. It all relates towards thinking and acting like human - that's why the penalties only apply towards humans. If it was health, then a draugr would be soulless and couldn't be diablerized (if we assume that diablerie requies a soul). And, to be frank, you can be soulless and still relate well to humanity. The state of your magical soul has little to do with it.<br /> <br /> Harmony reflects the balance between Flesh and Spirit. Not even human soul versus wolf spirit - the Flesh aspect includes the wolfy parts.<br /> <br /> Wisdom reflects a mage's control over their magic, not their soul. Hells, even ripping out your soul to make soul stones is only a risk to Mid Wisdom - you can literally throw your soul away in chunks and maintian a fair amount of Wisdom, but you automatically lose Willpower dots each time. Having a soul ripped out of you doesn't stop you from using magic until all your <i>Willpower</i> is gone.<br /> <br /> Changelings have shreds of human souls that are patched together by raw glamour and other bits of faerie stuff. Clarity, however, has nothing to do with the soul of a changeling, but how well they can differentiate stories and the hedge from reality. It lends itself to separating Hedge from reality, it works on detecting magic and other forms of perception ability. At no point is the soul involved.<br /> <br /> Cover has nothing to do with souls. Hells, even when you get a cover via soul pact, you <i>shove the soul out of the way and take everything else.</i> Buying a soul is solely for the purpose of getting rid of it. Primum is the pseudo-soul of demons, and it has its own stat independant of Cover.<br /> <br /> Satiety represents how hungry the Horror is. Which I suppose you could call it &quot;health&quot; since 0 Satiey means you're literally dying of hunger. But, in all other cases, especially in Astral combat, there's actual Health that represents how damaged the Beast's soul is.<br /> <br /> Calling Integrity-equivalents &quot;health of the soul&quot; is doesn't work. Its too different for everyone. Even if you want to argue that Humanity is a rotting human soul, that's too different from what everyone else measures to have any similarities. While Mage does touch on soul issues on occasion (thank you Reapers), for the most part its not a big deal. At best, its an Obsession for specific individuals and the hunt for a minor antagonist faction (one of dozens) with said obsession. The matter comes up in mortal games a bit more often, and Soul loss is a general mortal concern and not a Mage-specific one for a reason. That's why I think that Integrity is a measurement of the health of the soul - because the soul matters much more in a mortal game than it does in any other game.<br /> <br /> And that's why I think this entire thing is immaterial. So -what- if you don't have a human soul anymore? Barring individual ST/chronicle calls, souls are interchangable with no ill effect. We also know that souls leave the body and vanish upon death. The majority of vampires literally die before being revived - sometimes days - so its a huge question if its the same soul, a different soul, or a pseudo-soul taking its place. Human souls are like batteries that send a charge through the human's mind, giving them emotions and drive. The actual emotions and memories are just the actual circuitry that the charge runs through. If you swap out the battery for, say, a generator or a plug, the circuitry still runs. Most games only care about the circuitry. Diablerie could very well do the same - tossing out the actual soul (energy source) and only care about slaving the circuitry to the diablerist's circuits. At no point does the vampire care about the power source, the actual soul. As long as the circuits run, who <i>cares </i>how its powered? I'm sure many would love to know, but will it affect their day-to-day operations? That's more doubtful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-04-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:42:35-07:00","id":998222,"title":"","content":"Integrity-and-equivalents are a souls <i>health, </i>not its Health. They're a measure of functionality, not damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:49:31-07:00","id":998225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998122#post998122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that changelings had their souls ripped out by huntsmen as part of making their fetch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a tiny piece of it, according to the preview document.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998122#post998122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the horror is the beasts soul, satiety does describe the status of the beast's soul. Though describe it's hunger rather than it's health.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a being such as a Horror, where existence is defined by feeding, is there really a difference between hunger and health?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:23:44-07:00","id":998233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity measures how much empathy and perspective you have towards humans. It all relates towards thinking and acting like human - that's why the penalties only apply towards humans. If it was health, then a draugr would be soulless and couldn't be diablerized (if we assume that diablerie requies a soul). And, to be frank, you can be soulless and still relate well to humanity. The state of your magical soul has little to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Elfive says, the health of a soul doesn't have to measure its closeness to destruction. Instead, it's the souls general wellbeing and effectiveness. The loss of empathy for humanity could be an effect of the soul's decay. And a Draugur doesn't have to be soulless. Humans don't gain the Soulless Condition when their Integrity reaches zero, and Integrity quite explicitly measures the health of a human soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harmony reflects the balance between Flesh and Spirit. Not even human soul versus wolf spirit - the Flesh aspect includes the wolfy parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, so a healthy werewolf's soul is equal parts flesh and spirit, and certain behaviors can nudge it more towards coroporeality or ephemerality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom reflects a mage's control over their magic, not their soul. Hells, even ripping out your soul to make soul stones is only a risk to Mid Wisdom - you can literally throw your soul away in chunks and maintian a fair amount of Wisdom, but you automatically lose Willpower dots each time. Having a soul ripped out of you doesn't stop you from using magic until all your <i>Willpower</i> is gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, a human with the Soulless Condition doesn't lose Integrity either, at least not immediately. In fact, the Soulless Condition has an identical effect on Wisdom as it does on Integrity, so I'd say that's a pretty strong case for Wisdom having the same relationship with the condition of an Awakened soul as Integrity has with the condition of a sleeping soul. Again, the loss of control over one's magic is a side-effect of a Mage's soul being in poor condition. This is further supported by the fact that, yes, a Mage <i>does</i> need her soul to do magic; Mages with the Thrall Condition, the final stage of soul loss, cannot do magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings have shreds of human souls that are patched together by raw glamour and other bits of faerie stuff. Clarity, however, has nothing to do with the soul of a changeling, but how well they can differentiate stories and the hedge from reality. It lends itself to separating Hedge from reality, it works on detecting magic and other forms of perception ability. At no point is the soul involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't the changes wrought to a Lost soul change it such that, when healthy it keeps reality and fae in sharp relief and when unhealthy the lines blur? You say a Changeling's soul is a patchwork of human soul and Fae magic, maybe with high Clarity those soul components are separate and with low Clarity they blend into each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cover has nothing to do with souls. Hells, even when you get a cover via soul pact, you <i>shove the soul out of the way and take everything else.</i> Buying a soul is solely for the purpose of getting rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely the worst fit for the model. But I don't know, maybe the soul isn't necessarily thrown out, maybe the soul <i>is</i> the cover, or part of it is patched together with other souls to make a patchwork cover. Maybe Covers work because Angels sense &quot;being with a soul&quot; and assume that means not a Demon, since Demons don't have souls of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satiety represents how hungry the Horror is. Which I suppose you could call it &quot;health&quot; since 0 Satiey means you're literally dying of hunger. But, in all other cases, especially in Astral combat, there's actual Health that represents how damaged the Beast's soul is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as established I'm not talking about Health of the soul in the sense of measuring wounds and closeness to destruction. I'm talking about health more as in wellness, efficacy, and general soul-ish-ness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998220#post998220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling Integrity-equivalents &quot;health of the soul&quot; is doesn't work. Its too different for everyone. Even if you want to argue that Humanity is a rotting human soul, that's too different from what everyone else measures to have any similarities. While Mage does touch on soul issues on occasion (thank you Reapers), for the most part its not a big deal. At best, its an Obsession for specific individuals and the hunt for a minor antagonist faction (one of dozens) with said obsession. The matter comes up in mortal games a bit more often, and Soul loss is a general mortal concern and not a Mage-specific one for a reason. That's why I think that Integrity is a measurement of the health of the soul - because the soul matters much more in a mortal game than it does in any other game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, when we say &quot;soul&quot;, we're not necessarily talking about the thing Mages call souls. Vampires don't have those, or if they do, they're severely damaged. And I don't think it's necessarily a problem that the Integrity stats are so different, because the souls of different supernatural beings are also very different from each other. It follows logically that poor soul health would have vastly different effects on beings with vastly different souls, that function in different ways.<br /> <br /> Also, soul loss is just as much of a concern for Mages as it is for Sleepers. The Conditions have nearly identical effects on them. If anything, soul loss is harsher on a Mage because it also causes loss of Gnosis and eventual loss of all magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-04-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:12:29-07:00","id":998258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998233#post998233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div> Bwa? Sorry, but it just sounds like you're redefining &quot;soul&quot; for every game in a way that each game does not support. Especially for Demon - the game is pretty clear on that point. I just think you're forcing square pegs into round holes. Plus? Soul is a CofD core book concept and definition, not a Mage one, making it a concept that equally applies to all games.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I think this argument is more harmful than beneficial to the thread and the topic we're discussing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:30:04-07:00","id":998265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998258#post998258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Bwa? Sorry, but it just sounds like you're redefining &quot;soul&quot; for every game in a way that each game does not support. Especially for Demon - the game is pretty clear on that point. I just think you're forcing square pegs into round holes. Plus? Soul is a CofD core book concept and definition, not a Mage one, making it a concept that equally applies to all games.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I think this argument is more harmful than beneficial to the thread and the topic we're discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, side discussion on the nature of a soul are interesting, but largely irrelevant. We already know the soul is not the seat of who one really is, since they are interchangable. Whether a Vampire retains one or doesn't, doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> For the OP, the question is if the &quot;you&quot; died, but something that thinks it is you becomes a vampire, would becoming a vampire still be an attractive option.<br /> <br /> Personally, all opinion on the dreary plight of the Kindred besides, it actually <i>improves</i> the option. On the one hand, the singular you is now going through the Requiem, but in the proposed &quot;copy&quot; mechanism, there is now <i>another</i> you. Should one believe in an afterlife, you could be enjoying (or bemoaning) it, while your legacy doppelganger now wrestles with unlife. Best case scenario, the &quot;you&quot; gets resurrected, and now can get along with vampire you. Assuming, of course, you'd enjoy your own company, or find two (or more) of you a good thing.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the Star Trek transporter question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:32:49-07:00","id":998298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998265#post998265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, side discussion on the nature of a soul are interesting, but largely irrelevant. We already know the soul is not the seat of who one really is, since they are interchangable. Whether a Vampire retains one or doesn't, doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> For the OP, the question is if the &quot;you&quot; died, but something that thinks it is you becomes a vampire, would becoming a vampire still be an attractive option.<br /> <br /> Personally, all opinion on the dreary plight of the Kindred besides, it actually <i>improves</i> the option. On the one hand, the singular you is now going through the Requiem, but in the proposed &quot;copy&quot; mechanism, there is now <i>another</i> you. Should one believe in an afterlife, you could be enjoying (or bemoaning) it, while your legacy doppelganger now wrestles with unlife. Best case scenario, the &quot;you&quot; gets resurrected, and now can get along with vampire you. Assuming, of course, you'd enjoy your own company, or find two (or more) of you a good thing.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the Star Trek transporter question.</div> </div> </div> </div>This concept gets touched on the horror game SOMA as well. Basically, if something thinks it is you, has all your memories and personality, is it not you? In a world where vampires exist, I'd be a lot more willing to believe in the concept of an afterlife. Especially when a number of powers can interact with things like spirits, ghosts, and the underworld. So as you said, it seems like you'd be getting a best of both worlds situation (assuming you aren't opposed to the other banes of being a vampire such as blood and sunlight issues). Being aware of an afterlife to go to and having a body that is immortality. The qualm of something 'replacing you', but that is you, seems mostly a metaphysical concern at that point.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:35:57-07:00","id":998301,"title":"","content":"Its also the Hollow Mehket question! Goddess, those things were fun, but a pain in the ass to run!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:08:39-07:00","id":998319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998258#post998258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Bwa? Sorry, but it just sounds like you're redefining &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot; for every game in a way that each game does not support.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that maybe monsterhood redefines the soul. Maybe the fact that Requiem consistently referring to vampires' souls, which by the definition we see in Mage, they demonstrably don't have, isn't actually inconsistent. Maybe vampires' souls are different than mortal souls. And maybe that's also true of other monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998258#post998258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially for Demon - the game is pretty clear on that point. I just think you're forcing square pegs into round holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough in Demon's case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998258#post998258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus? Soul is a CofD core book concept and definition, not a Mage one, making it a concept that equally applies to all games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where exactly does the core book define a soul? The definition I'm aware of says they are made up of the five subtle Arcana and the Onerios is the inside of them. These are Mage concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998258#post998258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but I think this argument is more harmful than beneficial to the thread and the topic we're discussing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Sorry for the tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:30:00-07:00","id":998335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998319#post998319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where exactly does the core book define a soul? The definition I'm aware of says they are made up of the five subtle Arcana and the Onerios is the inside of them. These are Mage concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way back in the God-Machine Chronicle, p186 under Soul Loss it sort of gives some details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The human soul exists in Twilight (see p. 218) but is not made of ephemera, so is insubstantial even to ephemeral beings unless they have Numina or Influences allowing them to manipulate souls. In general, only very high-Rank ghosts, or angels specifically sent to meddle with souls, have such abilities. Some demons and mages also have the knowledge and power necessary to affect the higher self. The soul is so subtle, most people can\u2019t even tell that they have one \u2014 until it\u2019s gone. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-04-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:24:36-07:00","id":998374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998298#post998298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This concept gets touched on the horror game SOMA as well. Basically, if something thinks it is you, has all your memories and personality, is it not you? In a world where vampires exist, I'd be a lot more willing to believe in the concept of an afterlife. Especially when a number of powers can interact with things like spirits, ghosts, and the underworld. So as you said, it seems like you'd be getting a best of both worlds situation (assuming you aren't opposed to the other banes of being a vampire such as blood and sunlight issues). Being aware of an afterlife to go to and having a body that is immortality. The qualm of something 'replacing you', but that is you, seems mostly a metaphysical concern at that point.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>SOMA sadly shits its narrative bed because the way it shows its story to players makes the primary question it asks resolveable by an automated copy-paste function.<br /> <br /> As for this situation, nothing about it implies an afterlife, but nor does it imply your sense of self is tied to a soul or any other metaphysical characteristic. A vampire that is essentially a template-imprinted piece of darkness may still share continuity of consciousness with the original person and, thus, be them. Death may simply be absolute and total oblivion.<br /> <br /> As for a metaphysical concern, I'd say it is of immediate practical concern to me over whether I - to borrow a phrase - win the coin toss. Even if I assume that both continuities that result are equally me, one is going to experience some measure of psychological horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:54:01-07:00","id":998397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998374#post998374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SOMA sadly shits its narrative bed because the way it shows its story to players makes the primary question it asks resolveable by an automated copy-paste function.<br /> <br /> As for this situation, nothing about it implies an afterlife, but nor does it imply your sense of self is tied to a soul or any other metaphysical characteristic. A vampire that is essentially a template-imprinted piece of darkness may still share continuity of consciousness with the original person and, thus, be them. Death may simply be absolute and total oblivion.<br /> <br /> As for a metaphysical concern, I'd say it is of immediate practical concern to me over whether I - to borrow a phrase - win the coin toss. Even if I assume that both continuities that result are equally me, one is going to experience some measure of psychological horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might just be a personal opinion on the matter, but I think the afterlife is implied twofold in the situation. First, if I was to discover that vampire existed (explicitly being supernatural creatures with seemingly magical abilities), I'd probably be willing to start believing in other supernatural aspects of the world. Especially when said vampires can give me proof of the afterlife (via certain disciplines). Secondly, and more importantly, the scenario was presented with the thought that souls exist. If I were to think souls exist, then that even more-so would imply to me that there is an afterlife (that itself, while not inherent confirmation, would go a long way for me). If I don't think souls exist in the scenario period, then the point is moot, because the premise is based around your 'soul' being replaced by some sort of extra-dimensional entity.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to imply consciousness is tied to the soul either. Just that the point seems irrelevant as in the scenario, if it is tied, we have ways over varifying an afterlife, where we would go regardless. And if it isn't, then the soul is only of passing concern because you wouldn't necissarily need it if it wasn't tied in to who you are.<br /> <br /> As for which would have to suffer horror, everyone has to die someday (as far as basic humans are going). So if someone is making the decision to be a vampire with the understanding there is an afterlife, sure, you'd probably prefer to be the consciousness that remains in the body. But if you're going to die regardless, that's what seems to make it a lesser concern. Though, it might make being a ghoul the more appealing option.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T14:35:05-07:00","id":998438,"title":"","content":"Some spoilers for SOMA ahead, don't read if you want to play the game blind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998374#post998374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SOMA sadly shits its narrative bed because the way it shows its story to players makes the primary question it asks resolveable by an automated copy-paste function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I understand what you mean by this. I thought the way SOMA was presented was extremely effective, because it actually showed you what it would be like to learn that your consciousness is minutes old and all of your memories were from the life of someone else who is now dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998374#post998374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for this situation, nothing about it implies an afterlife, but nor does it imply your sense of self is tied to a soul or any other metaphysical characteristic. A vampire that is essentially a template-imprinted piece of darkness may still share continuity of consciousness with the original person and, thus, be them. Death may simply be absolute and total oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not the sense of self is tied to the soul is immaterial to the scenario presented in the opening post. In said scenario, the soul is destroyed, so <i>if</i> the soul is the seat of consciousness, your &quot;self&quot; is gone. Vampire's brains don't function, so if consciousness is a result of physiological processes, your &quot;self&quot; is still gone. The only way &quot;you&quot; persist in the presented scenario is if &quot;you&quot; are just the culmination of your memories, which YMMV, but I find to be a pretty horrifying thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998374#post998374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a metaphysical concern, I'd say it is of immediate practical concern to me over whether I - to borrow a phrase - win the coin toss. Even if I assume that both continuities that result are equally me, one is going to experience some measure of psychological horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. No matter what, one of &quot;you&quot; will die. But the thing is, in this scenario we know who wins the coin toss. The vampire does. Unless all the people on Pathos II who killed themselves after the brain scan were right and dying before your memories diverge from you copy's memories somehow preserves you, you're going to lose. Unless what you think you're experiencing right now is the vampire's memories, I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:51:44-07:00","id":998478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998397#post998397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be a personal opinion on the matter, but I think the afterlife is implied twofold in the situation. First, if I was to discover that vampire existed (explicitly being supernatural creatures with seemingly magical abilities), I'd probably be willing to start believing in other supernatural aspects of the world. Especially when said vampires can give me proof of the afterlife (via certain disciplines). Secondly, and more importantly, the scenario was presented with the thought that souls exist. If I were to think souls exist, then that even more-so would imply to me that there is an afterlife (that itself, while not inherent confirmation, would go a long way for me). If I don't think souls exist in the scenario period, then the point is moot, because the premise is based around your 'soul' being replaced by some sort of extra-dimensional entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, ghosts are explicitly not the person who died; just an imprint of them. Again, if an imprint is all that's necessary to be &quot;you&quot;, then that's just pedantry; merely a question of copying efficiency.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to assume that, because supernatural creatures exist, that the afterlife does, though. Just because vampires exist does not mean sasquatches do, or vice versa. There are a theoretically infinite number of possible supernatural beings and possible otherworldly existences and any one of them existing would not imply any other by necessity. It generates a general probability increase - magic existing makes the existence of other magical things more plausible - but the only reason to go &quot;Vampires, therefore afterlife&quot; is wishful thinking; the afterlife is more dear to us, so we are more likely to hope it exists than to, say, the assumption &quot;Vampires, therefore Loch Ness Monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998438#post998438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I understand what you mean by this. I thought the way SOMA was presented was extremely effective, because it actually showed you what it would be like to learn that your consciousness is minutes old and all of your memories were from the life of someone else who is now dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's the game's problem: It <i>doesn't</i> do that.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The big problem is that you, the player, are effectively the qualia of the protagonist; you are perceiving through his eyes, experiencing what he experiences. In a sense, you <i>are</i> his experiences because you take on the role of him. As such, the mechanics of the game tell us that we are the same person who walked into a doctor's office when we wake up an instant later elsewhere. When you transfer to the high pressure vessel and see your old self, you - the same person who has been playing the game and experiencing its story - see the old instance tied to a chair.<br /> <br /> Hence, SOMA's big problem: It <i>doesn't</i> depict the very thing it seems to be trying to depict. It shows a world in which consciousness is clearly able to be transferred on hard disk. Hence, the simple solution is to prevent instance issues; shut down, copy, paste. That way, there's no creation of two simultaneous but identical instances that can then diverge.<br /> <br /> SOMA doesn't show you that you're someone whose consciousness is minutes old; it shows you to be a guy in his (I think) late-twenties whose consciousness was forked, leading to two instances of his mind that diverged. You are one of those forks, but you have no less claim to that history than the other one because <i>you</i> were the one experiencing it before the forking.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998438#post998438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not the sense of self is tied to the soul is immaterial to the scenario presented in the opening post. In said scenario, the soul is destroyed, so <i>if</i> the soul is the seat of consciousness, your &quot;self&quot; is gone. Vampire's brains don't function, so if consciousness is a result of physiological processes, your &quot;self&quot; is still gone. The only way &quot;you&quot; persist in the presented scenario is if &quot;you&quot; are just the culmination of your memories, which YMMV, but I find to be a pretty horrifying thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not a vampire's brain functions, whatever spiritual substrate its mind runs on does a good job of mimicking the human brain enough that they think, feel, and act like human beings. They have a few instincts tweaked and changed but, then, so does a human on drugs. There's a pretty obvious comparison here to being uploaded into a computer, which, depending on your point of view, may be a very elaborate suicide or may be life everlasting.<br /> <br /> If the soul is the seat of your consciousness, though, and it is obliterated, then, yeah, tautologically, it's the end of your existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998438#post998438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. No matter what, one of &quot;you&quot; will die. But the thing is, in this scenario we know who wins the coin toss. The vampire does. Unless all the people on Pathos II who killed themselves after the brain scan were right and dying before your memories diverge from you copy's memories somehow preserves you, you're going to lose. Unless what you think you're experiencing right now is the vampire's memories, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the coin toss is that it's an inaccurate term. It's not &quot;real&quot; in a useful sense. Both instances are the <i>same</i> consciousness, diverging the instant the other one starts to run. If you shut down the consciousness, then instance it on a new platform, there is no divergence; it is the same consciousness that was there before. If you copy it a dozen times and instance all copies simultaneously, they are, for the first instant, the same consciousness.<br /> <br /> An easy way to think of this is to consider the transporter problem. The &quot;problem&quot; tries to demonstrate that transporters are a very elaborate form of suicide, because you can simultaneously instance a person in two locations at once and show somehow that they are not the same person.<br /> <br /> Yet consider a transporter that malfunctions in a different way. When it tries to teleport the person, it instead manages to create only an imperceptibly thin slice vertically down the person's centre, creating two identical mirror images of one another. The transporter, detecting an error, tries to correct the damage the only way it knows how. It scans each damaged half and then uses the same teleportation copying mechanisms to recreate the missing halves... But in doing so, it gets it wrong again; creating two new halves and attaching them to their respective complements. The result is two identical clones, each a perfect duplicate of the other, each with half of the original meat behind it.<br /> <br /> So which is the original consciousness?<br /> <br /> There are only two answers: They both are, or neither of them are.<br /> <br /> If they both are, diverging the instant of their forking, then you are forced to conclude that the idea of the coin toss is &quot;flawed&quot;. Copies are the same consciousness, which then begin to diverge. If you shut down the instance first before copying, there is no divergence and, hence, they are the same original consciousness.<br /> <br /> If neither is, you must provide a new mechanism by which continuity of self might be maintained, as you have refuted continuity of activity and of matter and of thought and memory.<br /> <br /> To turn this back to the point of the vampire, if you accept this idea of instanced consciousness, the new vampire is another instance of you. The idea that there is a distinction is just an argument over substrate. For all intents and purposes, the new vampire is little different from someone who just had their mind uploaded to a computer after the original instance died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:11:05-07:00","id":998508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998225#post998225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a being such as a Horror, where existence is defined by feeding, is there really a difference between hunger and health?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, a Horror could have just went through a big battle and only have 1 corpus left but still have 10 satiety. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:28:43-07:00","id":998539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998508#post998508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah, a Horror could have just went through a big battle and only have 1 corpus left but still have 10 satiety. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, health, not Health. General wellbeing, not physical (err... ephemeral?) damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:41:09-07:00","id":998731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998478#post998478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last I checked, ghosts are explicitly not the person who died; just an imprint of them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Acording to DaveB, 2e ghosts are people, not echoes. They don't have souls, but that doesn't stop them from being people. If that's not the same person who died, then it's kind of an argument over the definition of &quot;same person.&quot; (Much like the goal of this thread.) Rank 1 ghosts act stuck in a loop, but that's a, well, lets call it a ghostly equivalent of trauma mixed with a psuedo-coma. Those Rank 1 ghosts can be raised to Rank 2, who are fully aware, sapient, sentient and a bear the same personality and memories of the previous person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no reason to assume that, because supernatural creatures exist, that the afterlife does, though. </div> </div> </div> Indeed, no one knows what happens to souls after death, nor a ghost after it has &quot;moved on.&quot; Could be another plane of existance, could be oblivion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998539#post998539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, health, not Health. General wellbeing, not physical (err... ephemeral?) damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> A Horror's wellbeing is measured by several factors - Satiety (which is also its essence-equivalent), the size of its Lair, the health track, and more. Pretty much every Beast-specific mechanic on the character sheet is a measurement of the Horror's overall wellbeing. Satiety is part of it, but not the whole of it. Can we all agree on that at least?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:20:02-07:00","id":998750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998731#post998731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Horror's wellbeing is measured by several factors - Satiety (which is also its essence-equivalent), the size of its Lair, the health track, and more. Pretty much every Beast-specific mechanic on the character sheet is a measurement of the Horror's overall wellbeing. Satiety is part of it, but not the whole of it. Can we all agree on that at least?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we were abandoning this line of discussion because it wasn't relavent to the topic. But I would say Lair doesn't really track a Horror's wellbeing, so much as... err... the size of its Lair. And the health track doesn't track the sort of wellbeing I was talking about. It tracks actual injuries, not metaphysical wellness. I don't know Beast well enough to say with confidence whether or not Satiety is the only thing that tracks a Horror's metaphysical wellness, but those other two things are not what I was trying to describe with the word health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:05:36-07:00","id":998766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998731#post998731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Acording to DaveB, 2e ghosts are people, not echoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation needed, since I recall the exact opposite. Indeed, one of the examples was that you could have your <i>own</i> ghost as a familiar as a result of a near-death experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:22:05-07:00","id":998775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998766#post998766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, one of the examples was that you could have your <i>own</i> ghost as a familiar as a result of a near-death experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha woah, it's like a reverse Geist!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:29:52-07:00","id":998889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998766#post998766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citation needed, since I recall the exact opposite. Indeed, one of the examples was that you could have your <i>own</i> ghost as a familiar as a result of a near-death experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that Mages can create ghosts of people, even those still alive.<br /> <br /> Ghosts not being echoes contradicts so much fluff. I also find the suggestion hard to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:56:24-07:00","id":998925,"title":"","content":"What's to say echos can't be conscious individuals on their own? That a mage can create a ghost doesn't say much since they also can create spirits, goetia and even an independent consciousness.<br /> Think of ghosts as psychic echoes so strong they've become their own independent entities. Rank 1 ghosts are still stuck in a pattern, but they're more than just ephemeral residue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:48:57-08:00","id":999195,"title":"","content":"Here - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945621-why-is-immortality-such-a-big-deal?p=967238#post967238\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...238#post967238</a><br /> <br /> There are other posts floating around, talking about this rough subject. One, for instance, talks about how ghosts act like the living person would without a soul. You can warp ghosts with magic, do some crazy things, but that doesn't make them less people anymore than a soulless human isn't person.<br /> <br /> Calling a ghost an echo is disengenuous to the entire themes of Geist as well. You pretty much have a super-ghost in your head 24/7. Try telling one of the Bound that their Geister aren't people. Or any of the wretched beings in the Underworld trying to make an after-life bearable aren't people.<br /> <br /> Also remember that Mage, as a game, is set up so that you'll do bad things to people with your magic. Hubris and all that. So there's definitely an in-character bias and systemic prejudice / oppression against beings without a human soul. Werewolves and changelings are considered less of people than the most monstrous Sleeper. And supernal magic is arranged to encourage that exact kind of attitude towards other supernaturals. So, yeah. You get to do some rather twisted things to ghosts. You also get to do lots of bad things to living humans - to fellow mages - as well. Its easy to confuse the prejudice for cannon truth, but its not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-06-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:56:28-08:00","id":999244,"title":"","content":"That post seems to be saying exactly what Tessie said - just because they're echoes doesn't mean they're not people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:06:11-08:00","id":999245,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is the connotations of the word 'echo'; simple and mindless repetition. But 'echo' is just a thematic synonym for 'copy' in this context. And a copy certainly doesn't have to be lesser than the original. Just ask any geneticist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:20:22-08:00","id":999257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire#post917816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wondered lately why so many people wuldn't mind to become vampires, considering vampiric weaknesses and banes quite a reasonable price compared to eternal life, and was struck by one simple idea. And this idea was so cool and terrible, that I'd like to share it with you, for maybe in your setting you could put it into mouth of some Dragon scientist or Sanctified preacher (well, may be it already was in some manuals, I didn't read them all).<br /> <br /> When you are Embraced, you get immortality, right? Wrong. You just die. Forever. You lie still, cold, and your soul -- if you ever had one -- is forever gone.<br /> <br /> Then your Sire drops some Vitae in your mouth, and this Vitae holds some kind of mystical parasyte, that has no memory, no experience, just self-awareness. And as it fills your body, your brain, it devours your memory, your experience, your personality. It's not that you retain yourself, but get Beast into your soul. No. The Beast steals your body, your memories, your personality. It steals you whole and wears you like a masquerade costume. But as this Vitae-parasyte has no memories and personality of its own, it believes it being you.<br /> <br /> But you personally, you are dead, and gone forever. That's why spreading the Curse is not giving immortality. It is a murder.<br /> <br /> So. Do you still want to be a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but I'm entirely against this view of Vampires which by practice, it just makes the character a empty husk with a beast controlling it which is quite meaningless to play which going by this, they should be more like unplayable NPC antagonists if anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:39:58-08:00","id":999267,"title":"","content":"Well, that's basically what Draugr are, but that's not what the premise of this thread is. Whatever it is that's controlling the body still acts as a person. It still has Humanity because it has absorbed a human being and is acting out as that being since it believes it is that being.<br /> Also, the premise is for a thought experiment and discussion. I don't think it's meant to be applied when playing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:02:15-08:00","id":999277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999267#post999267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's basically what Draugr are, but that's not what the premise of this thread is. Whatever it is that's controlling the body still acts as a person. It still has Humanity because it has absorbed a human being and is acting out as that being since it believes it is that being.<br /> Also, the premise is for a thought experiment and discussion. I don't think it's meant to be applied when playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say if it was applied ingame which in pratice, it would render the entire purpose of the game moot and meaningless since it would ultimately derail and undermine the whole Personal Horror theme and the goal to maintain your humanity where it's implying that you never had in the first place when you were embraced therefore playing as something that never was human at all and it would make one look for alternatives for playing as a Vampire like supernatural while still being actually you rather than a beast controlled corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:19:27-08:00","id":999292,"title":"","content":"Let's say the players accepts this premise in a game: Wouldn't it become a new kind of personal horror trying to hold on to and even gain humanity in spite of not having been a human in the first place? A campaign played that way sounds a lot like the core premise of Promethean to me, complete with the potential of a happy ending if the ST allows PCs to reach Golconda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:34:18-08:00","id":999301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999292#post999292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say the players accepts this premise in a game: Wouldn't it become a new kind of personal horror trying to hold on to and even gain humanity in spite of not having been a human in the first place? A campaign played that way sounds a lot like the core premise of Promethean to me, complete with the potential of a happy ending if the ST allows PCs to reach Golconda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one of the reasons I would never accept this premise is because well, I would like to still have my own consciousness and even still having the essence of me rather than playing something that is pretending to be but really isn't.<br /> <br /> Also because I would exactly prefer Vampirism to actually grant immortality not murder as it's supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:47:16-08:00","id":999309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999301#post999301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well one of the reasons I would never accept this premise is because well, I would like to still have my own consciousness and even still having the essence of me rather than playing something that is pretending to be but really isn't.<br /> <br /> Also because I would exactly prefer Vampirism to actually grant immortality not murder as it's supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire is still conscious, and there's nothing to say that the vampire is actually pretending. It might actually be the person it believes it is. It's just that the memories comes from a previous iteration of that person.<br /> SOMA has already been brought up so I hope I don't spoil anything, but that game brings up the same philosophical problem. If all the memories and the personality of a person is scanned and then copied over to a computer in a robot body, won't that robot also be the same person, only a new iteration of them? It's not a perfect analogue to the premise of this thread (especially as the vampire is a modified cop), but it's the same concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:49:06-08:00","id":999310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999277#post999277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say if it was applied ingame which in pratice, it would render the entire purpose of the game moot and meaningless since it would ultimately derail and undermine the whole Personal Horror theme and the goal to maintain your humanity where it's implying that you never had in the first place when you were embraced therefore playing as something that never was human at all and it would make one look for alternatives for playing as a Vampire like supernatural while still being actually you rather than a beast controlled corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? In this hypothetical scenario, you are playing as the parasite that thinks it's human. For all you know, you did have Humanity and you do want to hold onto it. It functionally changes very little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:55:23-08:00","id":999315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999309#post999309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vampire is still conscious, and there's nothing to say that the vampire is actually pretending. It might actually be the person it believes it is. It's just that the memories comes from a previous iteration of that person.<br /> SOMA has already been brought up so I hope I don't spoil anything, but that game brings up the same philosophical problem. If all the memories and the personality of a person is scanned and then copied over to a computer in a robot body, won't that robot also be the same person, only a new iteration of them? It's not a perfect analogue to the premise of this thread (especially as the vampire is a modified cop), but it's the same concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think what the OP was implying that once you become a vampire, you actually die and move on to the afterlife therefore never experiencing yourself what is like to be a vampire while meanwhile if you're a ghost/wraith at all you look back and you see that <i>thing</i> that is now wearing your face and claiming to be you.<br /> <br /> While this might sound like a good horror idea but in pratice, it just doesn't work especially if one wanted to actually BE the vampire while still having your human soul but the beast is also there waiting to take over.<br /> <br /> Oh also in some Vampire folklore, it's implied that not only a Vampire has two hearts, they also have two souls as well which kinda plays into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:59:56-08:00","id":999319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999310#post999310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? In this hypothetical scenario, you are playing as the parasite that thinks it's human. For all you know, you did have Humanity and you do want to hold onto it. It functionally changes very little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Veindark's objections have to do with functionality (and mine certainly don't). To me, having the vampire be anyone but the original person who was embraced guts the entire notion of &quot;personal horror&quot; and eliminates pretty much all possible drama. You're no longer playing a character, you're playing a copy of a character who may or may not be considered to be a person, but you're not who you think you are.<br /> <br /> I think this kind of thing can be explored in some kinds of stories (like SOMA) but that in other stories it basically falls flat on its face (like Vampire). This is because of how such a thing would underscore or sabotage a game's themes. In a game like Vampire, if you were never human, your struggle for humanity is completely meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:05:56-08:00","id":999325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999315#post999315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this might sound like a good horror idea but in pratice, it just doesn't work especially if one wanted to actually BE the vampire while still having your human soul but the beast is also there waiting to take over.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't want to play something like that, then that's fine. I'm not going to argue about that. But I do want to point out that SOMA has proven that the concept does work in practice for other people, including me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:07:22-08:00","id":999327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999319#post999319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Veindark's objections have to do with functionality (and mine certainly don't). To me, having the vampire be anyone but the original person who was embraced guts the entire notion of &quot;personal horror&quot; and eliminates pretty much all possible drama. You're no longer playing a character, you're playing a copy of a character who may or may not be considered to be a person, but you're not who you think you are.<br /> <br /> I think this kind of thing can be explored in some kinds of stories (like SOMA) but that in other stories it basically falls flat on its face (like Vampire). This is because of how such a thing would underscore or sabotage a game's themes. In a game like Vampire, if you were never human, your struggle for humanity is completely meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:08:37-08:00","id":999328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999325#post999325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you don't want to play something like that, then that's fine. I'm not going to argue about that. But I do want to point out that SOMA has proven that the concept does work in practice for other people, including me.</div> </div> </div> </div>SOMA's a different sort of horror story, though. Requiem isn't SOMA and isn't really designed to work similarly. I enjoyed SOMA for being SOMA but I wouldn't enjoy a transplanting of its themes into Vampire simply because it worked great in one context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:10:42-08:00","id":999330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999319#post999319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this kind of thing can be explored in some kinds of stories (like SOMA) but that in other stories it basically falls flat on its face (like Vampire). This is because of how such a thing would underscore or sabotage a game's themes. In a game like Vampire, if you were never human, your struggle for humanity is completely meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be meaningless? I've already pointed out Promethean as a game line in CofD that already deals with the very same concept (sans that you've already adopted the memories and personality of a human). But I do agree Vampire is probably not the best game to play for that kind of scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:13:51-08:00","id":999332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999330#post999330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would it be meaningless? I've already pointed out Promethean as a game line in CofD that already deals with the very same concept (sans that you've already adopted the memories and personality of a human). But I do agree Vampire is probably not the best game to play for that kind of scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read Promethean as much as I've wanted to, so I couldn't really say one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:14:06-08:00","id":999333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999319#post999319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Veindark's objections have to do with functionality (and mine certainly don't). To me, having the vampire be anyone but the original person who was embraced guts the entire notion of &amp;quot;personal horror&amp;quot; and eliminates pretty much all possible drama. You're no longer playing a character, you're playing a copy of a character who may or may not be considered to be a person, but you're not who you think you are.<br /> <br /> I think this kind of thing can be explored in some kinds of stories (like SOMA) but that in other stories it basically falls flat on its face (like Vampire). This is because of how such a thing would underscore or sabotage a game's themes. In a game like Vampire, if you were never human, your struggle for humanity is completely meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't agree that it undermines the personal horror of vampire or invalidates the struggle for humanity. There are at least two Chronicles of Darkness game lines where you play as things that were never human and strive for humanity, and I dont think they are devoid of horror or that their conflict isn't meaningful. One of the overarching themes of Chronicles is that monsters can be people, even if they aren't human, and people can be monsters even if they aren't inhuman. If you're playing as a character who isn't human but doesn't know it, I don't see how your attempts to hold onto the things about yourself that you perceive as essential qualities of your humanity are in any way not meaningful. If anything, finding out that you're not human but persisting in trying to be so anyway just adds a tragic twist to it. It doesn't cheapen it.<br /> <br /> But that's just, like, my opinion, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:19:10-08:00","id":999337,"title":"","content":"Since people have brought up the &quot;that's kinda how it works in the Buffyverse&quot; argument, I'll just say I always found Spike to be significantly more compelling as a character before he got his soul back, and infinitely more than Angel ever was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:22:06-08:00","id":999339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999333#post999333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just don't agree that it undermines the personal horror of vampire or invalidates the struggle for humanity. There are at least two Chronicles of Darkness game lines where you play as things that were never human and strive for humanity, and I dont think they are devoid of horror or that their conflict isn't meaningful. One of the overarching themes of Chronicles is that monsters can be people, even if they aren't human, and people can be monsters even if they aren't inhuman. If you're playing as a character who isn't human but doesn't know it, I don't see how your attempts to hold onto the things about yourself that you perceive as essential qualities of your humanity are in any way not meaningful. If anything, finding out that you're not human but persisting in trying to be so anyway just adds a tragic twist to it. It doesn't cheapen it.<br /> <br /> But that's just, like, my opinion, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's unfair to compare Demon or Promethean to a bait and switch in Vampire, though. Vampire is neither Demon nor Promethean. And I just don't see how such a bait and switch is conducive to the kind of themes and drama that play out in Vampire. In Vampire you're trying to hold onto the person you were (at least to some extent) and not give in to the beast. This is not the same thing as playing a demon or promethean who are openly and explicitly &quot;never human.&quot; If a vampire is not really the person their appear to be then their struggles are simply meaningless. What are they trying to hold onto? What do their touchstones mean? All of that gets sidestepped and Vampire's themes get undermined if the characters were never human.<br /> <br /> There is no bait and switch in the other two games. You go in knowing what you're going to play and what that character's relationship to humanity is.<br /> <br /> I just don't see it as adding a tragic twist. I see it as <i>subtracting</i> all meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:24:40-08:00","id":999342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999337#post999337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since people have brought up the &quot;that's kinda how it works in the Buffyverse&quot; argument, I'll just say I always found Spike to be significantly more compelling as a character before he got his soul back, and infinitely more than Angel ever was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buffy is very different from Requiem, though. Vampires in Buffy don't struggle to hold onto their humanity and are all basically psychopaths. After the second season and for much of the first two seasons vampires are present primarily as easily dispatched minions with no moral complexity. There's nothing wrong with that in <i>Buffy</i> because that's a show about vampires being an evil scourge that the Slayer has to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:31:01-08:00","id":999346,"title":"","content":"And I am going to try to stay out of this thread, because clearly people enjoy the idea and that's not wrong, it's just not my cuppa tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:46:55-08:00","id":999354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999339#post999339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's unfair to compare Demon or Promethean to a bait and switch in Vampire, though. Vampire is neither Demon nor Promethean. And I just don't see how such a bait and switch is conducive to the kind of themes and drama that play out in Vampire. In Vampire you're trying to hold onto the person you were (at least to some extent) and not give in to the beast. This is not the same thing as playing a demon or promethean who are openly and explicitly &quot;never human.&quot; If a vampire is not really the person their appear to be then their struggles are simply meaningless. What are they trying to hold onto? What do their touchstones mean? All of that gets sidestepped and Vampire's themes get undermined if the characters were never human.<br /> <br /> There is no bait and switch in the other two games. You go in knowing what you're going to play and what that character's relationship to humanity is.<br /> <br /> I just don't see it as adding a tragic twist. I see it as <i>subtracting</i> all meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, but you're discussing it as if the players don't knowingly play a campaign where this premise is true. You'd have to work with different themes to make it work and not just slap it onto an ordinary vampire campaign that otherwise is straight from the book.<br /> You also assume the vampire is a new person with false memories while I can see the potential of the new entity being a new iteration of the same person, just like most people can do in SOMA. But even if we do assume this is a new person that does not have the right to the memories they've received, wouldn't that be potential for drama? Trying to cling on to humanity by using another person's memories. Interacting with a Touchstone still feels meaningful to your character, so is it wrong for your character to use a different person's life to become more human, or is your character unjustly using another person's life?<br /> The largest problem is that the vampire probably doesn't realize all this, but that's potentially another avenue for tragedy in this situation.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not saying it'll be a good game (in fact, I'm fairly certain it won't since VtR doesn't have the right tools for the concept) but I'm not agreeing with the reasons for outright dismissal.<br /> I don't feel I can explain my own opinion any clearer than this so I'll also stop posting for now. Also because I needed to get off my ass and start cooking some food an hour ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:54:56-08:00","id":999357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999339#post999339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's unfair to compare Demon or Promethean to a bait and switch in Vampire, though. Vampire is neither Demon nor Promethean. And I just don't see how such a bait and switch is conducive to the kind of themes and drama that play out in Vampire. In Vampire you're trying to hold onto the person you were (at least to some extent) and not give in to the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but (and this is the reason for the SOMA comparisons) if you share all of the memories and personality of the human who died, who is to say that that <i>isn't</i> the person you were? You can still hold onto the person you were in your memories, even if that person was a different entity at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999339#post999339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the same thing as playing a demon or promethean who are openly and explicitly &quot;never human.&quot; If a vampire is not really the person their appear to be then their struggles are simply meaningless. What are they trying to hold onto? What do their touchstones mean? All of that gets sidestepped and Vampire's themes get undermined if the characters were never human.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just that they appear to be that person, they <i>are</i> that person for all intents and purposes. Why isn't it meaningful to hold onto those memories? Why wouldn't your Touchstones be every bit as important to you, and keep you anchored to humanity just as much? I have seen plenty of assertions that those things are the case but I am at a complete loss for how or why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999339#post999339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no bait and switch in the other two games. You go in knowing what you're going to play and what that character's relationship to humanity is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. You'd go into this hypothetical vampire setting hack knowing what you're going to play too. Just because the character doesn't know they aren't human doesn't mean the player doesn't. It'd be kind of a dick move on the ST's part to spring such a setting hack on the players without running it by them first. Ideally before planning a chronicle around the it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999339#post999339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see it as adding a tragic twist. I see it as <i>subtracting</i> all meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is fine, but I don't understand where you're coming from with that. I don't see what about it subtracts meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999342#post999342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buffy is very different from Requiem, though. Vampires in Buffy don't struggle to hold onto their humanity and are all basically psychopaths. After the second season and for much of the first two seasons vampires are present primarily as easily dispatched minions with no moral complexity. There's nothing wrong with that in <i>Buffy</i> because that's a show about vampires being an evil scourge that the Slayer has to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Spike. Even when he was first introduced in season 2, he was a more nuanced character than any other vampire in the series. Sure, he was evil, but he was complex. You could empathize with him to a certain extent. Maybe not much until near the end of the season, but it was there enough, and went over well enough with the audience that they brought him back for a cameo in season 3 and then brought him back on permanently in season 4. And they played up the &quot;nuanced vampire&quot; angle even more, without having to resort to giving him a soul. He was undoubtedly a complete monster, but he was also a person, and that only made it all the more meaningful when he tried to be a <i>good</i> person. He failed. He was always doomed to fail, because at the end of the day he was still always a monster. But bless his heart, he <i>tried</i>. Just like a Requiem vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course, then they had to ruin it and give him a soul in season 7. But, at least they made it about just how much he failed at having a soul, instead of doing an Angel redux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:48:36-08:00","id":999520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999357#post999357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but (and this is the reason for the SOMA comparisons) if you share all of the memories and personality of the human who died, who is to say that that <i>isn't</i> the person you were? You can still hold onto the person you were in your memories, even if that person was a different entity at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not just that they appear to be that person, they <i>are</i> that person for all intents and purposes. Why isn't it meaningful to hold onto those memories? Why wouldn't your Touchstones be every bit as important to you, and keep you anchored to humanity just as much? I have seen plenty of assertions that those things are the case but I am at a complete loss for how or why.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean. You'd go into this hypothetical vampire setting hack knowing what you're going to play too. Just because the character doesn't know they aren't human doesn't mean the player doesn't. It'd be kind of a dick move on the ST's part to spring such a setting hack on the players without running it by them first. Ideally before planning a chronicle around the it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right, which is fine, but I don't understand where you're coming from with that. I don't see what about it subtracts meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>However the main point is that, you're not really playing as the same person who was Pre-Embraced but rather a beast possessed corpse on autopilot mode which therefore, you'll never really experience what it's like to be a vampire because the person is that is actually conscientiously you is now dead i.e. possibly a Ghost/Wraith floating around somewhere knowing the fact that <i>thing</i> is now inhabiting your body wearing you as a mask under this premise sort of like how a Changeling view their Fetch or the whole Doppelganger myth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999357#post999357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Spike. Even when he was first introduced in season 2, he was a more nuanced character than any other vampire in the series. Sure, he was evil, but he was complex. You could empathize with him to a certain extent. Maybe not much until near the end of the season, but it was there enough, and went over well enough with the audience that they brought him back for a cameo in season 3 and then brought him back on permanently in season 4. And they played up the &quot;nuanced vampire&quot; angle even more, without having to resort to giving him a soul. He was undoubtedly a complete monster, but he was also a person, and that only made it all the more meaningful when he tried to be a <i>good</i> person. He failed. He was always doomed to fail, because at the end of the day he was still always a monster. But bless his heart, he <i>tried</i>. Just like a Requiem vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course, then they had to ruin it and give him a soul in season 7. But, at least they made it about just how much he failed at having a soul, instead of doing an Angel redux.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spike is a bad comparison since you're also missing the point that the Vampires from Buffy were more like a &quot;Force of Nature&quot; with no free will of their own than actual monsters (due to being Demons) which Spike was no exception until Season 7 which the whole reason that happened was because his character became popular.<br /> <br /> This is the premise what the OP is proposing which falls flat due to this very reason since if you try to make Vampires like Buffy then it pretty much shoots itself in the foot with the personal horror theme where you character already has no free will of their own but rather it's just a beast possessing the corpse on autopilot mode well just like Buffy Vampires.<br /> <br /> For the reason why the Personal Horror theme would be rendered meaningless is that it would present the beast imitating their host's former personality, sharing it's host's memories, etc simply to lure their prey to their doom basically and they have no control over their actions which is where the other problem comes in which makes the whole struggle moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-06-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:05:22-08:00","id":999523,"title":"","content":"Basically, there are two ways this goes.<br /> <br /> One, it's as Charlaquin and others are saying; functionally, you are the same person, and you don't even know anything has changed. In this case, there's really no difference at all. It has no effect, for gameplay or otherwise, on the game. It's really a pointless and academic concept. You can't really do anything with the information that changes the game.<br /> <br /> In the other, you are aware of this fact. In this case, you're basically playing with Demon's themes, not Vampire's. You are a monster that took someone else's life as your own, trying to mimic it as best as possible. That's a fine theme, but it's already covered by Demon. Vampire has its own themes, and this concept damages those themes in favor of another line's themes. It's true that CofD covers these themes with some lines. That's perfectly fine, and I find those lines interesting for their own reasons. But Vampire is not Demon or Promethean. It's Vampire. And Vampire's mechanics and fluff should support its own themes, not another line's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:11:11-08:00","id":999527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999523#post999523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the other, you are aware of this fact. In this case, you're basically playing with Demon's themes, not Vampire's. You are a monster that took someone else's life as your own, trying to mimic it as best as possible. That's a fine theme, but it's already covered by Demon. Vampire has its own themes, and this concept damages those themes in favor of another line's themes. It's true that CofD covers these themes with some lines. That's perfectly fine, and I find those lines interesting for their own reasons. But Vampire is not Demon or Promethean. It's Vampire. And Vampire's mechanics and fluff should support its own themes, not another line's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda agree that both Vampire and Demon should stay seperate when it comes to their themes with the former actually being with now a inner monster clawing inside you that you must struggle against while the latter is actually about playing as that Demon possessing that corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:22:04-08:00","id":999530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999520#post999520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However the main point is that, you're not really playing as the same person who was Pre-Embraced but rather a beast possessed corpse on autopilot mode which therefore, you'll never really experience what it's like to be a vampire because the person is that is actually conscientiously you is now dead</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this &quot;beast&quot; that's possessing the corpse has no knowledge that it's possessing the corpse and isn't &quot;pretending to be you&quot; it is you. It has all your memories. It has all your personality. It has all your quirks. When there is no actual discernible or identifiable difference between &quot;Steve as a vampire&quot; and &quot;Vampire that has the mind and body of Steve&quot;, what makes the two not identical?<br /> <br /> Note: As far as science can tell, human bodies are already just organic machines running on auto-pilot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:25:48-08:00","id":999532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999520#post999520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However the main point is that, you're not really playing as the same person who was Pre-Embraced but rather a beast possessed corpse which therefore, you'll never really experience what it's like to be a vampire because the person is that is actually conscientiously you is now dead i.e. possibly a Ghost/Wraith floating around somewhere knowing the fact that <i>thing</i> is now inhabiting your body wearing you as a mask under this premise sort of like how a Changeling view their Fetch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was the point of the opening post, because the opening poster had an issue with the fact that their friends thought being a vampire would be cool and cooked this scenario up in an attempt to prove a point. But, people persisted in trying to engage with the premise as if it were a suggestion for an actual setting hack. And if you use the premise as a setting hack, you would be playing as the monster, not as the human. And if you're playing as a monster that thinks it's the human it replaced, that has all the same memories and personality as the person it replaced, then from the perspective of the character you are actually playing, that person may as well have been you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999520#post999520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spike is a bad comparison since you're also missing the point that the Vampires from Buffy were more like a &quot;Force of Nature&quot; with no free will of their own than actual monsters (due to being Demons) which Spike was no exception until Season 7 which the whole reason that happened was because his character became popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you <i>watch</i> Buffy? Spike's introduction to the show was him rolling in and killing vampire Jesus. He betrayed Angel and Drusilla because he didn't actually want to destroy the world. He came back to Sunnydale to abduct Willow and force her to do a love spell because he couldn't deal with the fact that Drusilla dumped him, and he called Buffy and Angel out on their toxic relationship while he was at it. He became friends with Joyce. He was downright parental towards Dawn. He nearly killed Drusilla to prove to Buffy that he loved her (an atrociously misguided gesture, but not something a demon with no free will would do). He refused to give up any information about Buffy or Dawn when Glory brutally tortured him. When the chip in his brain that kept him from hurting the living broke, Buffy (stupidly) trusted him enough to let the Initiative take it out without replacing it <i>and he didn't go back to killing people</i>. And finally, he sought out a way to get his soul back of his own volition. All of that happened before he had his soul back. If you think he didn't have a will of his own, you were not paying attention. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999520#post999520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the premise what the OP is proposing which falls flat due to this very reason since if you try to make Vampires like Buffy then it pretty much shoots itself in the foot with the personal horror theme where you character already has no free will of their own but rather it's just a beast possessing the corpse on autopilot mode well just like Buffy Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are deliberately ignoring the premise at this point. The monster thinks it is the same person as the human it replaced. It has the same memories and same personality. It does have free will, and it does want to hold onto the things that made the person it replaced human. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999520#post999520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the reason why the Personal Horror theme would be rendered meaningless is that it would present the beast imitating their host's former personality simply to lure their prey to their doom basically and they have no control over their actions which is where the other problem comes in which makes the whole struggle moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>When has anyone but you said the monster would have no control over its actions or that it would only be imitating human behavior to lure prey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-06-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:37:51-08:00","id":999534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999523#post999523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[if] it's as Charlaquin and others are saying; functionally, you are the same person, and you don't even know anything has changed. In this case, there's really no difference at all. It has no effect, for gameplay or otherwise, on the game. It's really a pointless and academic concept. You can't really do anything with the information that changes the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. The entire point of the opening poster's premise was that if it were true, would be no way for the vampire to know whether it was the human who's memories it had with eternal life, or a parasite that took over the human's body when it died. The premise was intentionally crafted in such a way as to be entirely irrelevant to actual gameplay, because they were trying to make a point about why real life people shouldn't want to be vampires, because you can't know you wouldn't actually just die and something identical to you wouldn't take over your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:33:30-08:00","id":999985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=998478#post998478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked, ghosts are explicitly not the person who died; just an imprint of them. Again, if an imprint is all that's necessary to be &quot;you&quot;, then that's just pedantry; merely a question of copying efficiency.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to assume that, because supernatural creatures exist, that the afterlife does, though. Just because vampires exist does not mean sasquatches do, or vice versa. There are a theoretically infinite number of possible supernatural beings and possible otherworldly existences and any one of them existing would not imply any other by necessity. It generates a general probability increase - magic existing makes the existence of other magical things more plausible - but the only reason to go &quot;Vampires, therefore afterlife&quot; is wishful thinking; the afterlife is more dear to us, so we are more likely to hope it exists than to, say, the assumption &quot;Vampires, therefore Loch Ness Monster&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure on the exact nature of ghosts in the setting. But I didn't mean to reference just ghosts in the 'vampire discpline' area, but the entire realm that is the Underworld as being rather compelling.<br /> <br /> I disagree as far as the scenario not giving rise to some reason to believe in an afterlife. I'm not saying that the existence of the supernatural confirms the afterlife exists. I tried my best to express that this was a personal assumption based on the scenario. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a world where vampires exist, I'd be a lot more willing to believe in the concept of an afterlife. </div> </div> </div> Again, not merely because vampires exist, but because of the fact that some of their magical abilities can directly interact with souls and reveal the existence of the Underworld.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:13:20-08:00","id":1000066,"title":"","content":"The Underworld contains ghosts, not souls. It is not an afterlife; it is simply a plane of existence which resonates with the echoes humanity makes upon death.<br /> <br /> As for souls, a vampire can indeed steal or even devour something which people <i>call</i> a soul, but if that soul is in any way connected to your conscious existence or any sort of afterlife, the setting is mum on it. After all, if a vampire steals and destroys your soul, you might not even actually <i>notice</i> at first. You'll eventually wind down into what amounts to exceptionally severe depression (there's insight, here, into the authors' views on mental illness, I am sure), but <i>you</i> still remain <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, none of these things give you any more reason to believe in the afterlife than anything else. The only reason they make you draw any sort of connection is because the word &quot;soul&quot; has been associated with the afterlife and the Underworld explicitly models itself off of humanity's ideas relating to death. If the soul was called the elan vital, you'd never associate it with any sort of afterlife, any more than you do Vitae. Death spirits model themselves off of humanity's ideas relating to death as well but no-one assumes they're actually psychopomps because we know it's just a spirit.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, in the Chronicles of Darkness, are <i>not</i> the person they resemble. They're just echoes. Ectoplasmic imprints a dying person makes on the fabric of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:19:32-08:00","id":1000108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1000066#post1000066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld contains ghosts, not souls. It is not an afterlife; it is simply a plane of existence which resonates with the echoes humanity makes upon death.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, now I'm confused. What the hell does World of Darkness define as a &quot;soul&quot; if it's not the disembodied spirit of someone who's physically dead?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999985#post999985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Again, not merely because vampires exist, but because of the fact that some of their magical abilities can directly interact with souls and reveal the existence of the Underworld.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except you'd actually have to be a vampire to make use of any of these powers. Or find a vampire willing to give you a demonstration. Which is nigh impossible, due to the masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:49:51-08:00","id":1000121,"title":"","content":"The 'soul' is part of a living being, or undead being in the case of vampires. It's in Twilight with you but otherwise doesn't do much except get hurt or strengthened by your actions. It's loss is represented by the Soulless Condition, but if ones soul is lost, it can be replaced by any soul, apparently.<br /> <br /> Sometimes ghosts are called 'souls' like in 'lost souls,' but they are not representative of the actual soul of a person. This has been discussed repeatedly across the board in various threads but it's easy to miss too.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem is that specifics of the soul are unknown, in-world, to most gamelines and it's been depicted in different forms, with different importance, in different games. In Mage and arguably vampire it's a source of power, but in mage it's also a bridge to the Astral, in Promethean it's part of an end-goal as they don't have souls but their condition is far worse than Soulless, in Demon it's an anchor for soul pacts and is, apparently, in Beast it's replaced by a Horror. None of these necessarily exclude the others, but each game usually describes them or their impact on things a bit differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:56:36-08:00","id":1000239,"title":"","content":"What Nofather said. Generally speaking, the soul is depicted as the magical equivalent to a thyroid gland; it regulates your emotional and spiritual health but is no more crucial to your personal identity than your liver or spleen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T06:49:11-08:00","id":1000248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1000066#post1000066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld contains ghosts, not souls. It is not an afterlife; it is simply a plane of existence which resonates with the echoes humanity makes upon death.<br /> <br /> As for souls, a vampire can indeed steal or even devour something which people <i>call</i> a soul, but if that soul is in any way connected to your conscious existence or any sort of afterlife, the setting is mum on it. After all, if a vampire steals and destroys your soul, you might not even actually <i>notice</i> at first. You'll eventually wind down into what amounts to exceptionally severe depression (there's insight, here, into the authors' views on mental illness, I am sure), but <i>you</i> still remain <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, none of these things give you any more reason to believe in the afterlife than anything else. The only reason they make you draw any sort of connection is because the word &quot;soul&quot; has been associated with the afterlife and the Underworld explicitly models itself off of humanity's ideas relating to death. If the soul was called the elan vital, you'd never associate it with any sort of afterlife, any more than you do Vitae. Death spirits model themselves off of humanity's ideas relating to death as well but no-one assumes they're actually psychopomps because we know it's just a spirit.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, in the Chronicles of Darkness, are <i>not</i> the person they resemble. They're just echoes. Ectoplasmic imprints a dying person makes on the fabric of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, these are not facts I'm trying to dispute. Merely that they'd give enough circumstantial evidence for me to feel sure enough about the situation. That supernatural (beyond even mundane supernatural) beings exist and ephemeral energy tied to your being exists. Those do give me more reason to believe in the afterlife here than in a world without them. The existence of other planes of reality is a compelling fact for me. Even with the fact that ghosts and souls are not the person with which they are associated, that would be enough to ignite my current lack of faith. Is it possible per the setting that ghosts, souls, other planes, etc exist entirely without any true afterlife for humans. But knowing about them would probably just add to my current belief system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:03:17-08:00","id":1000254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999244#post999244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That post seems to be saying exactly what Tessie said - just because they're echoes doesn't mean they're not people.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know. Others asked for me to provide citation for the idea that ghosts were people. So, I did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T22:00:20-08:00","id":1003248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=999532#post999532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that was the point of the opening post, because the opening poster had an issue with the fact that their friends thought being a vampire would be cool and cooked this scenario up in an attempt to prove a point. But, people persisted in trying to engage with the premise as if it were a suggestion for an actual setting hack. And if you use the premise as a setting hack, you would be playing as the monster, not as the human. And if you're playing as a monster that thinks it's the human it replaced, that has all the same memories and personality as the person it replaced, then from the perspective of the character you are actually playing, that person may as well have been you.<br /> <br /> You are deliberately ignoring the premise at this point. The monster thinks it is the same person as the human it replaced. It has the same memories and same personality. It does have free will, and it does want to hold onto the things that made the person it replaced human.<br /> <br /> When has anyone but you said the monster would have no control over its actions or that it would only be imitating human behavior to lure prey?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're also ignoring the point that if you play as the monster not the human then it makes the personal horror theme pointless and the humanity you have is really nothing more than a lie and the only way to be truly honest about yourself is to reach Draugrhood (Humanity 0) which is actually the <i>real you</i> and what you're <i>truly are</i> beneath that mask you call &quot;humanity&quot; sorta like a &quot;One Winged Angel&quot; equivalent to vampire which it's &quot;True Form&quot; <i>is</i> the Draugr itself.<br /> <br /> Also like I said, the monster has no free will since it plays along the lines of &quot;The person you once knew is dead, that thing is not your friend/family member/etc and it's only using you to put yourself in danger&quot;.<br /> <br /> So why does the monster itself want to hold unto the things that made the person it replaced human? In order to prolong the deception or it's hunting MO to lure it's prey or other words it's a wolf in sheep's clothing, nothing more and there's nothing less to relate to other than the lie it pretends to be which only creates a false sense of security.<br /> <br /> Hate to say this but if you can't play the human then Vampires should be casted as NPCs under this conclusion because there is no way would one to play and identify themselves with and as a monster itself living a lie much like a abuser presenting a false image whose power is dependent on their victim\u2019s psychological investment not their true selves which under this circumstance, if the vampire's true self is the beast then might as well stake it and leave it for the sunrise before it carries on hurting others as more people loose their lives.<br /> <br /> This is what Vampire should not be about in my opinion since it's just too nihilistically bleak and not very appealing to me and the game doesn't need anymore abuse metaphors than it already has like ghouls &amp; blood bonding for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T22:22:01-08:00","id":1003253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also ignoring the point that if you play as the monster not the human then it makes the personal horror theme pointless</div> </div> </div> </div>No one has yet explained how this is in any way the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the humanity you have is a lie and the only way to be truly honest about yourself is to reach Dragurhood which is the real you and what you're really are beneath that mask you call &quot;humanity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not a mask you call humanity, humanity is something you genuinely believe you have (or had). The fact that you are wrong about that doesn't change the fact that you think you are human and strive to be so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also like I said, the monster has no free will since it plays along the lines of &quot;The person you once knew is dead, that thing is not your friend/family member/etc and it's only using you to put yourself in danger&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way do you (the monster) not have free will? You keep making this claim but not providing any argument supporting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why does the monster itself want to hold unto the things that made the person it replaced human?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the hundredth time, because it thinks it is that person, it has that person's personality, and holding onto humanity is something that person would want to do, therefore it is something the monster would want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to prolong the deception or it's hunting MO to lure it's prey or other words it's a wolf in sheep's clothing, nothing more and there's nothing less to relate to other than the lie it pretends to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not consistent with the scenario presented in the opening post. You made this up yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate to say this but if you can't play the human then Vampires should be casted as NPCs under this conclusion because there is no way would one to play and identify themselves with and as a monster itself living a lie much like a abuser presenting a false image whose power is dependent on their victim\u2019s psychological investment not their true selves which under this circumstance, if the vampire's true self is the beast then might as well stake it and leave it for the sunrise before it carrys on hurting others it thrives on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're on about here. Could you rephrase this, because I can't follow it at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003248#post1003248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what Vampire should not be about in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scenario presented in the opening post doesn't really do much to change what vampire is about. It's still about monsters trying to cling to humanity. The difference is, by default the monsters used to be human, and in the proposed scenario the monsters only <i>think</i> they used to be human. But, since there's literally no way of telling if there is any continuity of consciousness between the people who died and the monsters they became, it makes absolutely no practical difference to the game. This is by design, because the opening poster was trying to make a point that people shouldn't want to become vampires because there's no way of proving, from the vampire's perspective, that their memories of life are really their own, and not the memories of a different person that they acquired when they took over the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-15-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:15:43-08:00","id":1003283,"title":"","content":"Note: The person you were a week ago is not actually the same person as you are now. You have that individuals memories, personality, and your body is basically the same. But your consciousness has been altered everytime you sleep and adjusted every time you even enter a different room and some of your cells have been replaced. Are you somehow a monster just pretending to be your old self just because you aren't the exact same?<br /> <br /> Also, how would you feel if you knew that even humans have no proof that we are actually making decisions, rather than our decisions actually all just being a result of neurochemical responses as a result of being just biological machines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-15-2016, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:43:50-08:00","id":1003317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003253#post1003253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one has yet explained how this is in any way the case.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Er, yes, we have. I certainly did. If this would be taken as truth, it removes pretty much all depth from playing Vampire. Everyone would be self-deluded monsters masquerading as people, rather than being people who have been made into monsters. There's no &quot;humanity,&quot; no &quot;there&quot; there. You may not <i>agree</i> with my points in this regard, but please don't claim I haven't answered that question. There's no point to the struggle for humanity when the humanity itself is an illusion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:50:40-08:00","id":1003318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003317#post1003317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, yes, we have. I certainly did. If this would be taken as truth, it removes pretty much all depth from playing Vampire. Everyone would be self-deluded monsters masquerading as people, rather than being people who have been made into monsters. There's no &quot;humanity,&quot; no &quot;there&quot; there. You may not <i>agree</i> with my points in this regard, but please don't claim I haven't answered that question. There's no point to the struggle for humanity when the humanity itself is an illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have at least three games that are already about being not humans and they still contain elements of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Simple fact is, it doesn't matter if your soul was switched out or not. Your soul is practically irrelevant. Your memories, experiences and personality are still the same and these are what makes your character what they are. If you were the person who balked at someone dying before you were Embraced, you were still that same person afterwards. Instead of Humanity being some metaphysical clinging to of human-ness, instead you have a more literal appreciation of what your character remembers as human-ness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:59:50-08:00","id":1003321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003318#post1003318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have at least three games that are already about being not humans and they still contain elements of personal horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of thought someone would bring this up. Each of those games has themes <i>consistent with not being or not having been human</i>. Promethean is about aspiring toward and eventually becoming human. Demon is about adopting human lives as cover, but not about actually being human. Vampire's themes put humanity and degeneration thereof front and center. If you were never truly human, the struggle is meaningless. It might look exactly the same as a vampire who was truly human before being changed, but I wouldn't play in such a game if I knew the GM was going to make a big deal about vampires not really being the people they're made from.<br /> <br /> There is no comparison between what the OP proposed for Vampire and how these other games approach humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simple fact is, it doesn't matter if your soul was switched out or not. Your soul is practically irrelevant. Your memories, experiences and personality are still the same and these are what makes your character what they are. If you were the person who balked at someone dying before you were Embraced, you were still that same person afterwards. Instead of Humanity being some metaphysical clinging to of human-ness, instead you have a more literal appreciation of what your character remembers as human-ness. </div> </div> </div>It was pointed out to me that the OP is not proposing the soul gets swapped out. We know that the soul isn't the seat of self, and I made that exact point earlier in this thread. Beasts are still themselves even though their human souls have been devoured and replaced with Horrors, while prometheans and demons don't even have souls. Having a soul or having a human soul isn't a central thing in the CofD, and isn't the point under discussion in this thread.<br /> <br /> If you are not really <i>you</i> which is the OP's point, then there's no &quot;there&quot; there, and there's no point to playing Vampire because the struggle for humanity is already lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:06:25-08:00","id":1003326,"title":"","content":"And I am not sure which game you mean as not being about having been human - I'm guessing Beast. Beasts simply don't have the same struggle with humanity that vampires do. There are issues with beast appetites if they don't feed regularly, and any given beast likely has a lot of hard questions to answer about what they're willing to do in order to feed, but degeneration isn't a central theme to the game, and wouldn't fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:14:27-08:00","id":1003331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003321#post1003321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of thought someone would bring this up. Each of those games has themes <i>consistent with not being or not having been human</i>. Promethean is about aspiring toward and eventually becoming human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Prometheans come from human stock, and in the fiction at least it's implied there's some memory seepage. Also werewolves, while once human, are no longer and deal with drastic changes in their lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon is about adopting human lives as cover, but not about actually being human. Vampire's themes put humanity and degeneration thereof front and center. If you were never truly human, the struggle is meaningless. It might look exactly the same as a vampire who was truly human before being changed, but I wouldn't play in such a game if I knew the GM was going to make a big deal about vampires not really being the people they're made from.<br /> <br /> There is no comparison between what the OP proposed for Vampire and how these other games approach humanity. </div> </div> </div>Actually there's quite a direct comparison between it and werewolf. As a werewolf you are not human. You are instead predator incarnate. And while clinging to humanity is a thing, it's a detrimental thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was pointed out to me that the OP is not proposing the soul gets swapped out. We know that the soul isn't the seat of self, and I made that exact point earlier in this thread. Beasts are still themselves even though their human souls have been devoured and replaced with Horrors, while prometheans and demons don't even have souls. Having a soul or having a human soul isn't a central thing in the CofD, and isn't the point under discussion in this thread.<br /> <br /> If you are not really <i>you</i> which is the OP's point, then there's no &quot;there&quot; there, and there's no point to playing Vampire because the struggle for humanity is already lost. </div> </div> </div>Except you are you. Everything that makes you you is still there. Your personality, memories, experiences, relationships, loves, hates, desires, wants. It's all the same as the character before they were Embraced. And there's no way to tell otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:16:35-08:00","id":1003333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003321#post1003321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you are not really <i>you</i> which is the OP's point, then there's no &quot;there&quot; there, and there's no point to playing Vampire because the struggle for humanity is already lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, a creature who isn't truly human (such as a parasite, demon, soulless automaton, est) could never be described as one. They are, at best, just an imitation trying to blend into their environment. They act human out of a desire for self preservation, and not because of any real empathy towards humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:55:58-08:00","id":1003392,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003333#post1003333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, a creature who isn't truly human (such as a parasite, demon, soulless automaton, est) could never be described as one. They are, at best, just an imitation trying to blend into their environment. They act human out of a desire for self preservation, and not because of any real empathy towards humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that's really fair. Non-human creatures don't have to be explicitly non-human and can be human-like. Parasites can possess empathy towards humanity as well. But the second issue, which I still haven't seem resolved (might've just missed it) is that, if they have all the same memories, personality, etc, how are they not fundamentally that person? At what point are you not you?<br /> <br /> As for lacking personal horror, something that thinks it is human can still strive to keep what 'humanity it has', when it has the memories and personality of a human. If I was playing a game and it was revealed my character was actually a clone, I'd hardly feel the effect of that characters journey was cheapened or that they aren't still clinging to what they think is their history. Just starts raising questions about what makes a human human to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:01:49-08:00","id":1003427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003392#post1003392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if that's really fair. Non-human creatures don't have to be explicitly non-human and can be human-like. Parasites can possess empathy towards humanity as well. But the second issue, which I still haven't seem resolved (might've just missed it) is that, if they have all the same memories, personality, etc, how are they not fundamentally that person? At what point are you not you?<br /> <br /> As for lacking personal horror, something that thinks it is human can still strive to keep what 'humanity it has', when it has the memories and personality of a human. If I was playing a game and it was revealed my character was actually a clone, I'd hardly feel the effect of that characters journey was cheapened or that they aren't still clinging to what they think is their history. Just starts raising questions about what makes a human human to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The thing about vampires is that the very nature of their existence causes whatever original personality they had to degrade. As time passes, they become jaded and cynical. How many times can you repeat the cycle of establishing friends and loved ones before their inevitable deaths (whether by old age, or less pleasant means) eventually causes you to stop trying?<br /> <br /> Even the Daeva, the most passionate of the clans, eventually loses that spark. Becoming as dead spiritually as they are physically.<br /> <br /> <br /> Assimilating a person's identity does not make you that person. It makes you an imitation, a copy, a thief. It doesn't matter if you have their soul, if they had to suffer (i.e die) for you to acquire it, then it means you stole what was theirs. Most vampires don't give their childer any choice in the matter. It's either 'I embrace you here and now' or 'I've revealed myself to you, now you have to die.'<br /> <br /> Or should we say that Fetches have the right to assume your identity after you've been kidnapped to a nightmare paradise and forced to do Lovecraft knows what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-15-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:21:15-08:00","id":1003435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing about vampires is that the very nature of their existence causes whatever original personality they had to degrade. As time passes, they become jaded and cynical. How many times can you repeat the cycle of establishing friends and loved ones before their inevitable deaths (whether by old age, or less pleasant means) eventually causes you to stop trying? </div> </div> </div>What you are describing can as much be called the nature of any immortal human, not necessarily that of a vampire. Anyone who outlives their friends and loved ones is going to e experience some level of reluctance to make bonds/withdrawn from humans. But that doesn't remove the ability for an immortal being, or a vampire, to have real empathy towards humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assimilating a person's identity does not make you that person. It makes you an imitation, a copy, a thief. It doesn't matter if you have their soul, if they had to suffer (i.e die) for you to acquire it, then it means you stole what was theirs. </div> </div> </div>But it continues to raise the question, what makes you, well, you? If not your personality and memories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or should we say that Fetches have the right to assume your identity after you've been kidnapped to a nightmare paradise and forced to do Lovecraft knows what? </div> </div> </div>No, but it also doesn't mean Fetches can't be, for certain purposes, considered to have some humanity, as it were. Or be able to relate to humans and their experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:22:17-08:00","id":1003437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003427#post1003427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assimilating a person's identity does not make you that person. It makes you an imitation, a copy, a thief. It doesn't matter if you have their soul, if they had to suffer (i.e die) for you to acquire it, then it means you stole what was theirs. Most vampires don't give their childer any choice in the matter. It's either 'I embrace you here and now' or 'I've revealed myself to you, now you have to die.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Beast isn't aware of any theft or stealing. You believe you're you and always have been. This may have happened to you, in real life, just last night, and there's no way to tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or should we say that Fetches have the right to assume your identity after you've been kidnapped to a nightmare paradise and forced to do Lovecraft knows what? </div> </div> </div>Fetches are an incredibly different scenario. For one thing, at least some of them know what they're doing. For another, at least some changelings have willingly given up their lives, which would forfeit your control over your life.<br /> <br /> If you want a better strawman you should have used vegetarians. Aside from being undead, the biggest shift in identity is a dietary one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:18:31-08:00","id":1003464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003317#post1003317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, yes, we have. I certainly did. If this would be taken as truth, it removes pretty much all depth from playing Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have only seen assertions, without supporting arguments. If it removes all depth, how does it do so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003317#post1003317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone would be self-deluded monsters masquerading as people, rather than being people who have been made into monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire is already about self-deluded monsters masquerading as people. The only difference this change makes is that the monsters didn't used to be human; a fact which we are informed of, but have no way of actually verifying, because they have a human's memories, thoughts, emotions, personality, everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003317#post1003317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no &amp;quot;humanity,&amp;quot; no &amp;quot;there&amp;quot; there. You may not <i>agree</i> with my points in this regard, but please don't claim I haven't answered that question. There's no point to the struggle for humanity when the humanity itself is an illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree because I haven't yet seen the logic that leads from the assumption, &quot;the character isn't really human&quot; and the conclusion, &quot;therefore there is no depth to playing the character.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:27:49-08:00","id":1003468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003333#post1003333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They act human out of a desire for self preservation, and not because of any real empathy towards humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly not the case in the scenario being discussed. They act human because they have the memories and personality of the human, and genuinely believe themselves to be that person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:32:57-08:00","id":1003472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003283#post1003283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: The person you were a week ago is not actually the same person as you are now. You have that individuals memories, personality, and your body is basically the same. But your consciousness has been altered everytime you sleep and adjusted every time you even enter a different room and some of your cells have been replaced. Are you somehow a monster just pretending to be your old self just because you aren't the exact same?</div> </div> </div> </div>^^^ This. You can't prove that the person who woke up in your bed this morning is the same &quot;person&quot; who went to sleep in it last night. The only evidence that can support the assumption that you are really &quot;you&quot; is your memories, and there is no way to prove they are actually your own. You could be some alien consciousness that killed the person who went to sleep in your bed, copied their memories, personality, and thought processes, and took control of their body. Does that make your life meaningless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-15-2016, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:44:44-08:00","id":1003479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003464#post1003464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree because I haven't yet seen the logic that leads from the assumption, &quot;the character isn't really human&quot; and the conclusion, &quot;therefore there is no depth to playing the character.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean would have some issue, if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:39:01-08:00","id":1003575,"title":"","content":"This thread is getting painful.... No, the vampire isn't pretending to be the person, they truly believe they are that person and there is literally no discernible difference between a Vampire that was the person and a Vampire with all it's personality/memories, that thinks it's that person. Stop using it in your arguments that it removes all the depth, as it is baseless. Your fine to say it's baseless, just please use an argument based on what's actually been proposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:09:20-08:00","id":1003592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003468#post1003468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is explicitly not the case in the scenario being discussed. They act human because they have the memories and personality of the human, and genuinely believe themselves to be that person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, yeah, but the fact remains that the person they are assimilating is dead. Whatever the CoD has for an afterlife, the human's remains have departed for it. The parasite forced itself upon them (unless the embrace was specifically romantic, and therefor under false pretenses). Just because it believes itself to be the person they killed does not excuse the fact they've killed somebody and assumed control over their lives.<br /> <br /> The only thing that would make this acceptable is if the person knowingly accepted the embrace without being coerced into it. They would freely surrender their identity to the thing taking over their body, and that is an extremely circumstantial scenario.<br /> <br /> And the very fact that it struggles to act human is proof that the assimilated identity would not be cool with this. It's horrified at the creature it's become, and struggles to keep it suppressed, or exorcise it from their body if possible. The original identity does not want to be inhabited by this thing inside of them. But if they do successfully purify themselves, that would mean getting rid of the parasite controlling them, and thus they return to being a lifeless corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-15-2016, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:25:43-08:00","id":1003607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003592#post1003592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because it believes itself to be the person they killed does not excuse the fact they've killed somebody and assumed control over their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this situation the Beast, what you call a parasite, didn't kill them. Their sire did. It's part of the Embrace, draining to death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing that would make this acceptable is if the person knowingly accepted the embrace without being coerced into it. They would freely surrender their identity to the thing taking over their body, and that is an extremely circumstantial scenario.<br /> <br /> And the very fact that it struggles to act human is proof that the assimilated identity would not be cool with this. It's horrified at the creature it's become, and struggles to keep it suppressed, or exorcise it from their body if possible. The original identity does not want to be inhabited by this thing inside of them. But if they do successfully purify themselves, that would mean getting rid of the parasite controlling them, and thus they return to being a lifeless corpse. </div> </div> </div>It likely struggles to act human for the same reasons vampires do. Despite having all the desires and memories and lifetime of experience of a human, they're a living corpse who burns upon exposure to sunlight and feasts for human blood.<br /> <br /> And there's actually six great coping mechanisms for adapting to it in the form of the covenants. The Lancea et Sanctum will tell you you've been given a mission from God, for instance. The Circle of the Crone a great gift. The Carthians believe you don't have to leave your humanity behind, and the Invictus has been living in structure for centuries. Also the Ordo Dracul strive to make things better, and Belial's Brood has a great crusade for you.<br /> <br /> There's also many other lesser-known groups out there offering people ways to deal with their new condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-15-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:33:07-08:00","id":1003609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003592#post1003592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, yeah, but the fact remains that the person they are assimilating is dead. Whatever the CoD has for an afterlife, the human's remains have departed for it. The parasite forced itself upon them (unless the embrace was specifically romantic, and therefor under false pretenses). Just because it believes itself to be the person they killed does not excuse the fact they've killed somebody and assumed control over their lives.<br /> <br /> The only thing that would make this acceptable is if the person knowingly accepted the embrace without being coerced into it. They would freely surrender their identity to the thing taking over their body, and that is an extremely circumstantial scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of this can't also be said about the Embrace in the default setting. Also, keep in mind that the character's sire thinks <i>it's</i> the person <i>it</i> replaced. Like, granted, the Embrace is a morally reprehensible thing, only made slightly more excusable if it's mutually consensual. Whether the consciousness of the human being embraced persists, or ends and is replaced with an identical consciousness doesn't change this fact at all, and makes only an academic difference at best, just like the question of whether your consciousness is the same as the consciousness of the person who went to sleep in your bed last night or a separate consciousness that is identical to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003592#post1003592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the very fact that it struggles to act human is proof that the assimilated identity would not be cool with this. It's horrified at the creature it's become, and struggles to keep it suppressed, or exorcise it from their body if possible. The original identity does not want to be inhabited by this thing inside of them. But if they do successfully purify themselves, that would mean getting rid of the parasite controlling them, and thus they return to being a lifeless corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, none of this isn't also true of the default setting. The Man struggles against the Beast. Whether or not the Man shares continuity of consciousness with the human who was embraced is immaterial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:31:09-08:00","id":1003639,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a><br /> <br /> Except that all of those covenants exist to serve the interest of vampires, not humanity. The Circle of the Crone worships ancient, pagan deities (or even portrays themselves as one). They conduct blood sacrifices and preach that vampires are a part of the natural world (and therefor such a parasite should be accepted, not rejected). The Lancea Sanctum are the vampire equivalent to the <i>Westboro Baptists</i>. The Invictus' structured order has always and will always exist solely for the benefit of the elders who run the show. They don't give a crap about the ones who serve under them, unless it specifically inconveniences their own plans. The Carthians are about adapting to the modern era, which does not necessarily mean keeping in touch with their humanity. It simply means they know how to adapt to the changing times. The Ordo Dracul conduct experiments that would cause any mortal to be stripped of their medical license or kicked out of the scientific community. And the Brood... well they just tell you to flat out abandon your human identity and embrace the Beast in all its glory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Except that in the default setting, there's no parasite involved. You're not the vampire pretending to be Dan, you're Dan the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-15-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:54:54-08:00","id":1003651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003639#post1003639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>Except that all of those covenants exist to serve the interest of vampires, not humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite true. They all serve as a reason to keep Humanity, and as a method for doing so, even Belial's Brood doesn't just drop down to draugr. They are there to serve the interests of their members, who are vampires.<br /> <br /> I hope you're not referring to humanity with a little h, as whether or not the organizations benefit humankind have no bearing on how human they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Circle of the Crone worships ancient, pagan deities (or even portrays themselves as one). They conduct blood sacrifices and preach that vampires are a part of the natural world (and therefor such a parasite should be accepted, not rejected). The Lancea Sanctum are the vampire equivalent to the <i>Westboro Baptists</i>. The Invictus' structured order has always and will always exist solely for the benefit of the elders who run the show. They don't give a crap about the ones who serve under them, unless it specifically inconveniences their own plans. The Carthians are about adapting to the modern era, which does not necessarily mean keeping in touch with their humanity. It simply means they know how to adapt to the changing times. The Ordo Dracul conduct experiments that would cause any mortal to be stripped of their medical license or kicked out of the scientific community. And the Brood... well they just tell you to flat out abandon your human identity and embrace the Beast in all its glory. </div> </div> </div>Eh, you should read up on these before generalizing, but you've got the gist. Either way, that's what it takes. A vampire can't just live a normal human life anymore no matter how much they try. So they have formed special groups to help each other out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-15-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:11:42-08:00","id":1003657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003639#post1003639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that in the default setting, there's no parasite involved. You're not the vampire pretending to be Dan, you're Dan the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you can't prove that with in-character information alone. Second of all, you're not pretending to be Dan in the proposed scenario either. You have Dan's body, Dan's soul, Dan's memories, Dan's personally, Dan's thought processes, Dan's temperament, Dan's likes and dislikes... There is no objective quality that separates you from Dan. The only reason we even know you're not Dan is that we are informed so for the purposes of the thought experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:18:09-08:00","id":1003658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003657#post1003657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, you can't prove that with in-character information alone. Second of all, you're not pretending to be Dan in the proposed scenario either. You have Dan's body, Dan's soul, Dan's memories, Dan's personally, Dan's thought processes, Dan's temperament, Dan's likes and dislikes... There is no objective quality that separates you from Dan. The only reason we even know you're not Dan is that we are informed so for the purposes of the thought experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Except the OP asked if we would have agreed to become a vampire if this is how it worked. And I would strongly say NO to such a process. I would not want to be embraced unless I personally get to enjoy the benefits of it. If all I'm doing is jumping ship and letting something else hop in the captain's seat, then becoming a vampire is absolutely not worth it. And if I had some way of cheating death, you can bet I'd be coming back for my body. Whether to resume control of my life, or destroy the thing that took my place.<br /> <br /> The only one who has permission to be me, <i>is me.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-15-2016, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:42:28-08:00","id":1003667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003658#post1003658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the OP asked if we would have agreed to become a vampire if this is how it worked. And I would strongly say NO to such a process. I would not want to be embraced unless I personally get to enjoy the benefits of it. If all I'm doing is jumping ship and letting something else hop in the captain's seat, then becoming a vampire is absolutely not worth it. And if I had some way of cheating death, you can bet I'd be coming back for my body. Whether to resume control of my life, or destroy the thing that took my place.<br /> <br /> The only one who has permission to be me, <i>is me.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that is precisely the purpose of the thought experiment. If you would not say yes to this deal, you should not say yes to the Embrace, because it is impossible to prove it doesn't work that way. It was never meant to be engaged with as an element of actual gameplay, because it is intentionally designed in such a way as to be utterly indistinguishable from the default setting from the perspective of the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:06:10-08:00","id":1003738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003464#post1003464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only seen assertions, without supporting arguments. If it removes all depth, how does it do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have made supporting arguments. I made supporting arguments in the post you just responded to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003464#post1003464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is already about self-deluded monsters masquerading as people. The only difference this change makes is that the monsters didn't used to be human; a fact which we are informed of, but have no way of actually verifying, because they have a human's memories, thoughts, emotions, personality, everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire is about people who were once human struggling to retain their humanity. When you remove the &quot;once human&quot; part, it completely changes the context. Vampires are <i>not</i> deluded about having been human, at least in the default setting. Vampires per the OP's proposal <i>are </i>deluded about having been human.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the &quot;no way of actually verifying&quot; thing is overplayed, because people who object to this idea are objecting from the position of players and storytellers, not from the position of in-game characters. If I know, as a player, that my character was never really human and is just a parasite who's stolen human form, memories, personality, then there's nothing there for me to play because it ain't Vampire. I would not play in such a game, and I would quit and leave if this were introduced as a truth of the setting after the game started. I don't want to play a Vampire game like that because there's no personal horror in such a revelation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't agree because I haven't yet seen the logic that leads from the assumption, &quot;the character isn't really human&quot; and the conclusion, &quot;therefore there is no depth to playing the character.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I would disagree that you haven't seen the logic. You have seen it, even in the post you responded to here. You may not <i>agree</i> with it, but that does not make it absent.<br /> <br /> But I'll say it one more time: If the character was never human, the struggles aren't real. It's a sham, a con, at best a bait and switch. You're going to play Vampire! No, wait, you're actually going to play a game where vampires were never human, and have no true connection to humanity, making a mockery of the emphasis on humanity, degeneration, and touchstones. Your character isn't who they appear to be and never was. Your character is <i>completely</i> delusional about who and what they really are. It's great if you want a game where the characters are pod people, but I don't think Vampire should be that game.<br /> <br /> And I mean games where you play pod people have their place, and have their own horror, hence SOMA. I mean SOMA practically tells you what's going on early on, so it's not even a surprise.<br /> <br /> I think the questions as to whether we're the same people after we sleep and wake up are irrelevant. I mean I guess it's useful for someone to debate that idea but I think it's pretty much a non-starter. That comic strip with the alien going on about humans only living for 16 hours at a time just struck me as being about an arrogant alien fucking with a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-15-2016, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:21:56-08:00","id":1003742,"title":"","content":"And I guess I should add <i>de gustibus non est disputandum</i>. I think the question as to whether anyone has sufficient logic to convince you that this is a bad idea is also completely irrelevant. Some people (like myself) really dislike this idea, and that's all the justification I need for disliking it: I don't like what it would do to my perception of Vampire as an RPG. No one needs a more substantial reason than that. If you think I'm here to convince you to think as I do about this, then you're wrong. I am trying to explain why I don't like it, and it is pretty frustrating to be told that my reasons for not liking an idea are not good enough. I don't need to justify myself with a full dissertation. Nor does Veindark or Nyrufa or anyone else who dislikes the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:28:12-08:00","id":1003745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003331#post1003331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually there's quite a direct comparison between it and werewolf. As a werewolf you are not human. You are instead predator incarnate. And while clinging to humanity is a thing, it's a detrimental thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is like vampire - you are a person, a human, who has become a monster. Werewolf doesn't explore the lost humanity element in the same way as Vampire because it sets out to do different things, however I wouldn't exactly care for a version of werewolf where a spirit bonds itself to your body and hollows you out to make room for itself to assume your life and identity, either. I wasn't saying that playing characters who aren't human is bad or playing characters who were never human is bad, I am saying playing a Requiem (or Masquerade) <i>vampire</i>, specifically, who was never human is completely uninteresting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003331#post1003331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you are you. Everything that makes you you is still there. Your personality, memories, experiences, relationships, loves, hates, desires, wants. It's all the same as the character before they were Embraced. And there's no way to tell otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made this point to Charlaquin, but no one is talking about this from the perspective of <i>being</i> a vampire, or at least I haven't seen it. I am, at least, talking about this from the perspective of a player or ST (more likely to ST than play) for whom this particular take is an automatic dealbreaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T20:40:05-08:00","id":1003764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want to play a Vampire game like that because there's no personal horror in such a revelation. </div> </div> </div>If you don't like that style of horror, that's fine. But there is personal horror in such a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T00:28:44-08:00","id":1003802,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised people don't think that there is personal horror in the curiosity about whether or not you are truly you. I've seen it done rather well in fiction, where the protagonist doesn't know if he is the first or just thinks they're a real-person (Fullmetal Alchemist as a great example of this for a manga aimed at 14 year olds there are also some films that are rather good at this but generally that element ends up being a plot twist so using them as examples would diminish the work abit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-16-2016, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T00:54:02-08:00","id":1003808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003802#post1003802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised people don't think that there is personal horror in the curiosity about whether or not you are truly you. I've seen it done rather well in fiction, where the protagonist doesn't know if he is the first or just thinks they're a real-person (Fullmetal Alchemist as a great example of this for a manga aimed at 14 year olds there are also some films that are rather good at this but generally that element ends up being a plot twist so using them as examples would diminish the work abit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd say that's one of the weaker elements of FMA. I mean, it's kinda interesting for a few minutes, but it has pretty much no impact on the world. It's like, to use charlaquin's example, are you the same person when you wake from sleep? It doesn't really matter, you still need to sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:13:26-08:00","id":1003815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003808#post1003808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd say that's one of the weaker elements of FMA. I mean, it's kinda interesting for a few minutes, but it has pretty much no impact on the world. It's like, to use charlaquin's example, are you the same person when you wake from sleep? It doesn't really matter, you still need to sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it has more impact than that since it means that their have been major lies and deception by people that you trusted most and it creates a lot of angst for him. Also if it is true or not has ramifications on how souls work in the setting which.... is sorta a big thing in Fullmetal Alchemist.<br /> <br /> And um... the sleep thing gets used as an example Because it pretty much has no impact on the world. It's purely academic and there is literally no difference if it ends up being true or false. Exactly like This Thread's Proposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T05:54:28-08:00","id":1003881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003764#post1003764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like that style of horror, that's fine. But there is personal horror in such a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>A kind of personal horror that isn't <i>Vampire</i>. It works in John Dies at the End to some extent, but Vampire isn't pod people horror whereas pod people are all over JDatE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:02:03-08:00","id":1003884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003802#post1003802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised people don't think that there is personal horror in the curiosity about whether or not you are truly you. I've seen it done rather well in fiction, where the protagonist doesn't know if he is the first or just thinks they're a real-person (Fullmetal Alchemist as a great example of this for a manga aimed at 14 year olds there are also some films that are rather good at this but generally that element ends up being a plot twist so using them as examples would diminish the work abit).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I noted in previous posts, pod people horror does work, it's just that Vampire is not a pod people game. Or rather, I don't think itshould be a pod people game. All horror isn't interchangeable with all other horror. Just because identity horror works in Full Metal Alchemist or SOMA doesn't mean that identity horror works in every single work of horror. This is why demons and prometheans not being human is irrelevant to the question of whether vampires were at one point human, or why werewolves are better able to deal with turning into a monster without degenerating than vampires are. Each of these game lines is about a particular kind of entity, and it doesn't really make sense to say &quot;since demons were never human, then vampires can be like that too and it'll work smoothly.&quot; It won't, as evidenced by people in this thread reacting badly to the idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:14:57-08:00","id":1003889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003881#post1003881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A kind of personal horror that isn't <i>Vampire</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's why it's a hypothetical scenario responding to people who've said they would become a vampire in 'real life' if the offer was extended to them using Vampire the Requiem terms.<br /> <br /> And not an actual game. Or a homebrew. Or even a suggestion for a game.<br /> <br /> You keep insisting that it would be different from the viewpoint of the Storyteller or Player, but that's not what the question was about in the first place. It was asking if you, whatever your real name was, would take the offer knowing this.<br /> <br /> And as pointed out, repeatedly, you would not notice any difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:25:40-08:00","id":1003896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003889#post1003889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. That's why it's a hypothetical scenario responding to people who've said they would become a vampire in 'real life' if the offer was extended to them using Vampire the Requiem terms.<br /> <br /> And not an actual game. Or a homebrew. Or even a suggestion for a game.<br /> <br /> You keep insisting that it would be different from the viewpoint of the Storyteller or Player, but that's not what the question was about in the first place. It was asking if you, whatever your real name was, would take the offer knowing this.<br /> <br /> And as pointed out, repeatedly, you would not notice any difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're shifting goalposts - the conversation has covered a lot of ground, <i>including</i> the possibility of this being a thing in games. Since no one in this thread is ever going to be a vampire, the question as to whether a real person would accept existence as a vampire is irrelevant. On the other hand, whether this premise would be acceptable in a Vampire <i>chronicle</i> is definitely on point since I would assume many people in this discussion have played or will play Vampire: The Requiem.<br /> <br /> I don't even want to be having this conversation again. The only reason I jumped back into the thread was because Charlaquin said no one had explained why this idea doesn't work for Vampire, which was not true. What <i>is</i> true is that reasonable people may differ, but that doesn't make my objections wrong. They're certainly absolutely correct for me, even if they're not true for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:57:37-08:00","id":1003913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003881#post1003881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A kind of personal horror that isn't <i>Vampire</i>. It works in John Dies at the End to some extent, but Vampire isn't pod people horror whereas pod people are all over JDatE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't what you said in what I quoted. Saying you dislike the personal horror and thinking it isn't fitting of Vampire is one thing. Saying there is no personal horror in such a concept is another.<br /> <br /> As for it not fitting Vampire, I'd contest that as well. Putting aside that Vampire can, as written/intended, fit almost any horror without putting it in a box, it focuses on horror over one's deeds and one's self. Typically this can involve losing your humanity, frenzying, fitting the beast in with your desire to maintain normalicy, etc. But the entire body switcher situation doesn't invalidate it, merely alters it some. You'd still be struggling to hold on to your identity (which would be you at that point), adjusting to your increasingly horrific situation, and such. You're still realizing you are the monster, just a slightly more alien one than you might have originally realized. It doesn't make the struggles any less real as the character still has an identity they hold as who they are. They do still have a connection through their memories, personality, and likely their friends/family who they still view a connection with.<br /> <br /> Again, if you dislike that sort of personal horror, that's valid. But it is there and it can fit Vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:59:21-08:00","id":1003916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003884#post1003884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I noted in previous posts, pod people horror does work, it's just that Vampire is not a pod people game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally a game about corpses clinging onto warped vestiges of humanity because they can never truly be what they once were. They are now forever an inhuman mockery of what they once were, sure vampires pretend to be civilised in their courts but all kindred know that the beast lies stirring just below the surface..... no, I think this is a game that would fit identity horror pretty well.<br /> <br /> Though to be honest, I don't see why talking about whether &quot;identity-horror&quot; works for vampire is relevant, since that's not the type of horror this would put on people since the characters have no way of knowing such a thing in character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason I jumped back into the thread was because Charlaquin said no one had explained why this idea doesn't work for Vampire, which was not true. </div> </div> </div>No one's said any reason why it doesn't work for vampire without using the &quot;pretending to be the person&quot; argument, which isn't really what is proposed (especially the &quot;pretending to be the person so it can lure in prey&quot; one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-16-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:15:34-08:00","id":1003976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003896#post1003896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you're shifting goalposts - the conversation has covered a lot of ground, <i>including</i> the possibility of this being a thing in games. Since no one in this thread is ever going to be a vampire, the question as to whether a real person would accept existence as a vampire is irrelevant. On the other hand, whether this premise would be acceptable in a Vampire <i>chronicle</i> is definitely on point since I would assume many people in this discussion have played or will play Vampire: The Requiem.<br /> <br /> I don't even want to be having this conversation again. The only reason I jumped back into the thread was because Charlaquin said no one had explained why this idea doesn't work for Vampire, which was not true. What <i>is</i> true is that reasonable people may differ, but that doesn't make my objections wrong. They're certainly absolutely correct for me, even if they're not true for you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not shifting the goalposts at all, that's literally what the opening post was about. If anything, the insistence on engaging the subject as something meant for actual play is a shift from the actual topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:22:41-08:00","id":1004021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire?p=1003916#post1003916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...since the characters have no way of knowing such a thing in character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really enjoyed your post. Quoting this little bit because it may or may not be true. If it is true or false in a particular Chronicle, there very well may be ways to confirm or deny the hypothesis. Given the plethora of powers for divining truths, and possible experiments those could be coupled with, I think it is is premature to claim it'd be <a href=\"https://philosophynow.org/issues/57/How_Can_I_Know_Anything_At_All\" target=\"_blank\">unknowable</a>. What is more important is figuring out which version is true in the Chronicle you're running and its repercussions, in case you have an inquisitive player who'd like to solve and exploit the mystery, or you'd like to display an NPC who has and its fallout as a plot. Compelling stories are available either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-16-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:08:46-08:00","id":1004184,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":".  Trying to be done with this discussion 11-16-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:16:58-08:00","id":1004186,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-16-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:19:46-08:00","id":1004189,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-16-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}